{"parentUuid":"8eec36c7-90ce-4933-bc57-858c68b55919","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgkpcn2spobhDT7RmsjLp","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01HtLHVdY7i77NoWHpH7jRBz","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"D=/Users/kenneth/.claude/projects/-Users-kenneth-Projects-JusPrin/memory; for f in ux-walkthrough-real-app-recipe scratch-app-driving-traps live-test-built-app-on-mac fake-host-page-fixture screenshots-to-files-via-page-fixture real-app-signed-in-without-screen-control open-file-in-app-without-screen-control drive-app-with-posted-key-events; do echo \"=== $f\"; cat $D/$f.md | sed -n 1,60p; done"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":444,"cache_read_input_tokens":247208,"output_tokens":482,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":28},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":444,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":482,"cache_read_input_tokens":247208,"cache_creation_input_tokens":444,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":444},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01HtLHVdY7i77NoWHpH7jRBz":{"command":"D=/Users/kenneth/.claude/projects/-Users-kenneth-Projects-JusPrin/memory; for f in ux-walkthrough-real-app-recipe scratch-app-driving-traps live-test-built-app-on-mac fake-host-page-fixture screenshots-to-files-via-page-fixture real-app-signed-in-without-screen-control open-file-in-app-without-screen-control drive-app-with-posted-key-events; do echo \"=== $f\"; cat $D/$f.md | sed -n 1,60p; done"}},"apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CgkpcmnjoWaLrzKFoUsJZ","requestRef":"96e9db9b-6211-4bb1-96c0-473c538688fc","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","attributionMcpServer":"ccd_session","attributionMcpTool":"start_session","type":"assistant","uuid":"458dd890-02fe-4e4d-a92e-9475a062dc26","timestamp":"2026-11-06T01:39:56.039Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/.claude/projects/-Users-kenneth-Projects-JusPrin/figma-mirror","sessionId":"473348c5-5f94-4e4d-9ad9-c7e9dd10b438","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"jusprin-newui","slug":"glimmering-doodling-lovelace"}
{"parentUuid":"458dd890-02fe-4e4d-a92e-9475a062dc26","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"ecb09a06-cb84-4541-b46c-4a925331f135","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HtLHVdY7i77NoWHpH7jRBz","type":"tool_result","content":"=== ux-walkthrough-real-app-recipe\n---\nname: ux-walkthrough-real-app-recipe\ndescription: \"How to drive the real built JusPrin app for a screenshot-per-step UX walkthrough (2026-10-28): scratch copies, the empty local_machines loop with the fake printer, why background app_* tools fail on Orca dialogs, and where screenshots land.\"\nmetadata:\n  node_type: memory\n  type: project\n  originSessionId: 33551592-d22c-4161-9a14-9a22ef798541\n  modified: 2026-10-28T13:12:42.393Z\n---\n\nOn 2026-10-28 I walked six scenarios (open-and-print, fix-a-problem) through the real app with Opus 5.5 and published the critique at https://claude.ai/artifact/XyVvteGiKhiJ6apUx8rcmR (34 frames, scratch copy at scratchpad/ux/ of that session). Kenneth's steer: start from files people actually download (MakerWorld 3MFs carry a full Bambu profile: printer, print preset, filaments, colours, bed type, designer, licence), not from generated STLs. `~/Downloads` has Tape_4_3MF.3mf (A1 mini profile), find_my_hollow.3mf (P1S, 3 colours, 233 mm wide, too big for an A1 mini), arrow_headband.3mf (P1S), general_purpose_hook.STL (bare).\n\n**Recipe that worked**\n- `ditto` the built .app out of `build/arm64/src/RelWithDebInfo/` into the scratchpad before launching (another session's ninja can relink it underneath you); the bundle id is already unique (`io.jusprin.JusPrin`), no re-sign needed.\n- `ditto` `~/Library/Application Support/JusPrin2` to a scratch `--datadir`; set `jusprin.fake_printer=true`, `presets.machine` to the saved \"Bambu Lab A1 mini 2\", write `jusprin/fake_printer.json`, delete `jusprin/mcp.json.lock`.\n- **Clear `local_machines`.** Kenneth's conf carries a `local_machines` entry keyed by the empty string (old Moonraker experiment). With the fake Bambu agent on, `init_networking_callbacks`' connect callback calls `DeviceManager::set_selected_machine(\"\")` in a loop (\"same lan machine, dev_id =, disconnect and reconnect\"), the main window disappears and the log grew 700 MB in two minutes. Clearing the map fixed it. The loop has no guard; see [[fake-bambu-printer-sim]] and [[harness-fake-printer-cleanup]].\n- Background `app_*` tools cannot press OrcaSlicer's custom `Button`s (no AX action) and the hit test at the dialog's screen position reports \"belongs to a different process\". `request_full_control` + `computer_batch` works for everything, including the Agent web view and the macOS file chooser (`cmd+shift+g`, type the path, Return, Return). Re-front the app with `open_application` when another session's harness steals focus.\n- Every `app_screenshot`/`computer_batch` screenshot is written as a JPEG under `~/.claude/projects/<project>/<session>/tool-results/mcp-computer-use-blob-*.jpg`; copy those for a report instead of fighting `screencapture`.\n- The dev build (-O0) slices a 38 mm part in over a minute; wait 45–60 s before judging a slice.\n\n**Why:** the first launch attempt looked like an app bug (blank window, title \"Couldn't save\") and cost ten minutes; the dialog-click refusals cost another ten.\n**How to apply:** reuse this for any \"walk through the app as a user\" request; keep scenarios on downloaded files; write the critique per step as what the person knows / sees / finds confusing. Related: [[live-test-built-app-on-mac]], [[drive-app-with-posted-key-events]].\n=== scratch-app-driving-traps\n---\nname: scratch-app-driving-traps\ndescription: \"Five traps met driving a scratch copy of the built app without screen control (2026-11-04): in-place binary copy gets SIGKILL, Home drops bridge messages while hidden, header popups need a posted NSEvent, lldb std::string args, wx Wrap reuse.\"\nmetadata:\n  node_type: memory\n  type: reference\n  originSessionId: dea8379c-b02c-43a2-a254-4c2259672439\n  modified: 2026-11-04T18:59:38.548Z\n---\n\nMet while verifying print-host printer window fixes on the scratch `.app` (see [[live-test-built-app-on-mac]], [[open-file-in-app-without-screen-control]]).\n\n- **Copy a new build into a `.app` with `rm` then `cp`.** `cp` over the existing signed binary keeps the inode; the kernel kills the launch at once (exit 137, nothing logged).\n- **A launch from a plain Bash call dies when the call ends.** Start the app with `run_in_background: true` and `exec`.\n- **Home ignores bridge messages while the main window shows a project.** A queued `launch_monitor` through `JUSPRIN_HOME_DEV_URL` is sent by the page and silently dropped; switch to Home first (`m_tabpanel->SetSelection(0)` via lldb).\n- **Background `app_click` does not reach the header's popup menus** (they are not listed as windows). Post the click into the app's queue with lldb: `expr -l objc -- @import AppKit`, then `NSEvent mouseEventWithType:NSEventTypeLeftMouseDown/Up location:NSMakePoint(x, y-from-popup-bottom) ... windowNumber:[popup windowNumber]` and `[NSApp postEvent:atStart:NO]`. Render the popup with `cacheDisplayInRect:` on its contentView ([[capture-mac-popups-for-platform-diff]]).\n- **lldb cannot build `std::string` args.** This libc++ uses the alternate short-string layout: a 24-byte char array with the text at offset 0 and its length in byte 23 (≤ 22 chars), passed as `*(std::string*)buf`.\n- **wx `wxStaticText::Wrap()` (Orca's wx) skips a width it already wrapped at and keeps the first text it wrapped**, so SetLabel + Wrap on a reused label comes back unwrapped. Use a fresh label.\n=== live-test-built-app-on-mac\n---\nname: live-test-built-app-on-mac\ndescription: \"How to launch, see, and drive the locally built JusPrin app on the Mac: the shared bundle id binds tools to the wrong instance, and \\\"on another Space\\\" usually means the window is on the second monitor, not that the user is in full screen.\"\nmetadata: \n  node_type: memory\n  type: project\n  originSessionId: fa2d66ed-e217-440b-aae0-da4164953edc\n  modified: 2026-11-01T19:29:08.107Z\n---\n\nEvery build of the fork (and /Applications/OrcaSlicer.app) shares bundle id `com.softfever3d.orca-slicer`. The desktop-control tools resolve an app by bundle id and bind to whichever instance comes first, so `app_list_windows` returns `[]` and filtered screenshots hide the window you actually launched.\n\n**Working recipe (2026-09-05):** `ditto` the built .app into the scratchpad, `plutil -replace CFBundleIdentifier -string com.jusprin.worktree-test`, `codesign --force --deep -s -`, then `open -n <copy>.app --args <model>` and `request_access` for the new id. `app_screenshot`/`app_click` then work and include popup menus. A display-scope `left_click` on the header did NOT open the fork's PopupWindow menus, but a background `app_click` did; take the pixel-level `zoom` with the display tools afterwards (call `app_release` first). Display-scope `Escape` does not close those popups; a click elsewhere does.\n\nThe MCP discovery file `~/Library/Application Support/JusPrin2/jusprin/mcp.json` points at the newest instance's `http://127.0.0.1:<port>/mcp`; `tests/mcp/probe.py`'s `call()` can drive real tools (e.g. `workspace_inspect`, then `report_slice_review` with sessionId/plateId/sliceResultId) to put the header into the Check-print state without lldb. lldb `expr` cannot call inline accessors like `status_row()`.\n\n**Why:** On 2026-09-01 a verification pass screenshotted the stock app instead of the build; on 2026-09-05 the tools bound to another session's main-repo build.\n\n**How to apply:** Confirm the pid with `pgrep -fl OrcaSlicer.app/Contents/MacOS`; never kill an instance you did not launch. `osascript` System Events by unix id still works to set `frontmost`. See [[jusprin-shell-phase-1-design]] and [[orca-inherited-teardown-crash]].\n\n**\"On another Space\" usually means \"on the other monitor.\"** Cost about ten turns on\n2026-09-09 and produced a wrong report to Kenneth. `app_list_windows` returns\n`is_off_space: true` and clicks are refused with \"this window is on another Space\";\n`app_bring_to_current_space` then fails with \"the user's current Space is a full-screen\napp.\" Both messages are about Spaces, so the natural read is that the user is sitting in\na full-screen app — but with *Displays have separate Spaces* on, a window merely sitting\non the second monitor produces exactly the same symptoms. Kenneth was not in full screen;\nthe harness had opened on the Acer.\n\nTell them apart before saying anything to the user: take a **display-scope** screenshot\n(`app_release`, then `computer_batch` screenshot). Its header names the monitor it\ncaptured and lists the others — if the window shows up there, it is a monitor problem,\nnot a Space problem, and the display-scope tools can drive it immediately. Never conclude\n\"the user is in a full-screen app\" from the background tools' error text alone.\n\nThe same flag also flaps: a window can read `is_off_space: false` and click fine, then\nread `true` a minute later. Clicks delivered while it is true report `ok ... unverified`\nand silently do nothing. **A click that reports \"unverified\" and changes nothing is not\nevidence of an application bug** — on 2026-09-09 that nearly became a filed defect about\nbeing unable to retry after a failed MCP connect. Re-verify on a reachable window before\nconcluding anything about the app.\n\n**Prefer the shell harness over a re-signed app copy for Agent-panel work.**\n`tests/shell/.../JusPrinShellHarness.app` already carries its own bundle id\n(`io.jusprin.shell-harness`), so none of the bundle-id collision above applies, and\n`--manual-unconfigured` lands directly on the dock's not-set-up state — one click from\nthe Agent setup chooser. Build target is `shell_integration_harness`, not `shell_harness`.\n\n**Isolate `$HOME` when testing MCP client setup.** `Mcp::default_catalog_paths()` reads\n`$HOME`, so the flow will happily rewrite the real `~/.cursor/mcp.json`. Launch with\n`HOME=<scratch>` holding a `.cursor/mcp.json` fixture; detection, the diff, and the write\nall follow it. Force a write failure with `chmod 444` on the file **and** `555` on its\ndirectory — the directory alone is not enough.\n\n**Re-signed copies trigger system prompts.** Each rebuild + ad-hoc re-sign changes the cdhash, so macOS re-asks for Downloads access (recent-project thumbnail load blocks in `fopen`) and Keychain access (agent runtime reads the API key). Both are prompts only the user can answer. Avoid them by running the binary directly (`nohup <copy>.app/Contents/MacOS/OrcaSlicer --datadir <scratch copy of JusPrin2 with recent_projects cleared> <model>`) with `OPENAI_API_KEY=<placeholder>` in the environment, which short-circuits the Keychain lookup in `AgentConfiguration.cpp`. Use `sample <pid>` on the main thread to see which prompt is blocking.\n\n**Stale as of 2026-09-18 (branch claude/printer-conversation-panel-af11cb):** `load_agent_runtime` reads the key only from app config (`jusprin_agent` / `openai_api_key`); no env var or Keychain lookup exists there. In the shell harness, `OPENAI_API_KEY` only feeds the docked pane via `install_harness_agent`; the printer panel builds its own runtime from app config, so `--printer-live` writes the key into the run's throwaway conf. Pass it as `std::string`: `AppConfig::set(section, key, const char*)` silently picks the `bool` overload and stores `true` (seen as a 401 \"key rejected\"). The harness temp data dir then holds the real key: delete `/var/folders/*/*/T/jusprin-shell-*` dirs from those runs afterwards.\n\n**Hands-on printer panel with a live model (2026-09-23, jusprin-newui, uncommitted at the time):** `--manual-live-agent` now also writes `OPENAI_API_KEY` into the run's app config, so Home → \"+ Add printer\" gets a live printer chat. Feed the key from `~/Library/Application Support/JusPrin2/JusPrin2.conf` (`jusprin_agent.openai_api_key`) via env without echoing it. Drive it with display-scope `computer_batch` clicks/typing (background `app_click` does nothing on the web view). The scripted `--printer-live` run hangs when the model doesn't pick the printer its next \"tap\" step expects; kill it. Afterwards `rm -rf` the run's `/var/folders/*/*/T/jusprin-shell-*` dir — killed runs leave it behind with the key.\n\n=== fake-host-page-fixture\n---\nname: fake-host-page-fixture\ndescription: \"Render the built AgentUI/HomeUI bundles in the built-in browser with a scripted fake native host, to see page states the live app makes hard to catch\"\nmetadata: \n  node_type: memory\n  type: reference\n  originSessionId: 9bb21a20-a19f-4500-adcf-139798a1201d\n  modified: 2026-09-19T16:55:23.039Z\n---\n\nBoth pages find their host through `window.wx.postMessage(json)` and receive host\nenvelopes through `window.__jusprinBridge.deliver(envelope)` (`WebShared/bridgeClient.ts`).\nCopy `resources/jusprin/{agent,home}/index.html` to a scratch dir, inject\n`<script>` right after `<head>` that (1) defines `window.wx` answering `hello` with\n`hello_ack` + a full `state`, and (2) exposes `window.fake.deliver(type, payload)`;\nserve with `python3 -m http.server` and open `agent.html?panel=printer` /\n`home.html` via `preview_start`. Drive it with `javascript_tool`: deliver\n`assistant_started` with no `assistant_delta` to freeze a streaming empty turn,\n`printer_session` to pin a card, `printer_added` for Home's receipt strip. A file\ndrop works with `new DragEvent('drop', {dataTransfer})` on `.app--printer`.\nEnvelope: `{protocol:'jusprin-agent-bridge'|'jusprin-home-bridge', version:1, id, type, payload}`.\nUsed 2026-09-19 to review branch these-commits-are-probably-wrong in ~10 minutes.\n\n**Why:** the desktop tools were locked by another session and background\n`app_click` never reaches WKWebView content, so page-level states (streaming\nactivity line, compact photo chip, leave dialog, receipt strip) had no other cheap\nproof. It proves page rendering only; host behaviour (e.g. the 256 KiB image\npreview cap `kInlineImagePreviewCap` in `AgentHost.cpp`) must be replicated in\nthe fake by hand or checked live.\n\n**How to apply:** reach for this before building a full app + datadir copy when the\nquestion is \"what does the page draw for state X\". Pair with [[live-test-built-app-on-mac]]\nfor the host side. Related: [[render-widget-to-bitmap-for-visual-proof]].\n=== screenshots-to-files-via-page-fixture\n---\nname: screenshots-to-files-via-page-fixture\ndescription: \"computer_batch save_to_disk produced no files (2026-09-23); to get screenshot files for a report, replay the observed host state into the built Agent/Home page under Playwright, which saves PNGs; plus the window-overlap trap when another session runs the harness.\"\nmetadata:\n  node_type: memory\n  type: project\n  originSessionId: 49ad3806-419d-49f2-8833-1578cd5bf2b3\n  modified: 2026-09-23T21:16:58.377Z\n---\n\nOn 2026-09-23 a full live walkthrough of the printer panel was driven with display-scope `computer_batch` (`zoom` + `save_to_disk: true`). Every call returned the image, but no path was reported and a disk-wide search found no file. Do not count on `save_to_disk` for deliverables.\n\n**What worked for files:** the [[fake-host-page-fixture]] recipe under the Playwright MCP. Copy `resources/jusprin/agent/index.html` (and `home/index.html`), inject `window.wx` + a `window.SCENES` table of full `state` payloads, serve with `python3 -m http.server`, open `agent.html?panel=printer`, switch scenes with `browser_evaluate` and save with `browser_take_screenshot` (`scale: device`, `filename` under the repo's `.playwright-mcp/`, the only allowed root; move the PNGs out and `rm -rf .playwright-mcp` afterwards so `git status` stays clean). Real printer pictures come from `resources/profiles/<Vendor>/<Model>_cover.png` as data URLs. The credential card renders from a `toolActivities` entry with `tool: 'printer_connect'`, `correlationId` = an assistant message id, state `pending` (card) or `succeeded` (\"Sent\"). Chips come from a trailing `Choices: a | b` line. 13 scenes took about 10 minutes and matched the live rendering.\n\n**Window overlap trap:** when another session runs `JusPrinShellHarness --printer-live` in a loop, each run opens a 1200x800 window at the same origin (360,125) on the primary display and takes the front, so display-scope zooms and clicks land on *its* window. Move your own instance by pid with a 20-line Swift AX helper (`AXUIElementCreateApplication(pid)` → `kAXPositionAttribute`) onto the built-in display (bounds start at y=1080 here), then `switch_display \"Built-in Retina Display\"`. The first display click only focuses the window; click again. `--manual-live-agent` does not enable the fake Bambu printer, so the Bambu connect path is out of reach in manual mode.\n\n**Why:** the walkthrough's evidence would otherwise have been lost, and a click into the other session's scripted run could have corrupted its result.\n\n**How to apply:** for any \"take screenshots\" request on the web pages, plan on the fixture route for files from the start and use the live app only to observe. See [[live-test-built-app-on-mac]] and [[printer-live-harness-lessons]].\n=== real-app-signed-in-without-screen-control\n---\nname: real-app-signed-in-without-screen-control\ndescription: \"Drive the real app signed in to a local gateway through an injected page script; which conf keys, why a copied binary dies, and what still needs the screen.\"\nmetadata:\n  node_type: memory\n  type: reference\n  originSessionId: f57d8b7e-fd5a-4daf-9378-2e3d21342f7c\n  modified: 2026-11-02T13:45:04.141Z\n---\n\nBuilds on [[live-host-check-via-instrumented-dev-page]]; used 2026-11-02 when screen control of the app was denied.\n\n- Signed-in conf needs all of: `jusprin_agent.{provider=jusprin, jusprin_api_key, enabled=true, cloud_consent=true, jusprin_model_formats=<JSON id→format from GET /ent/jusprin/v2/models>}`, `jusprin_server.base_url`, `jusprin_onboarding.status=completed`. Without the formats the Agent says \"not set up\".\n- An installed printer is `\"models\":[{\"vendor\":\"Custom\",\"model\":\"Generic Klipper Printer\",\"nozzle_diameter\":\"0.4\"}]`, not `vendors`.\n- Kill the app before editing the conf. Replace a scratch binary with `rm` then `cp`: `cp` over a binary that has run gets the new process killed at launch.\n- `Contents/Resources` in the build is a symlink to the worktree. Replace it with a real folder of links before corrupting a resource, or the worktree gets corrupted.\n- Bringing the app forward triggers an account refresh, so to race the gateway (a real 402), change the ledger and send without refocusing.\n- Page text input: native value setter plus an `input` event. A modal Preferences window's page polls as `agent-preferences`.\n- A test preset needs a `version` field or import rejects it.\n- A compose recreate drops env set by a wrapper; check `JUSPRIN_MODEL_ALIASES` before any chat so only the fake upstream is reachable.\n\nStill needs the screen: pointer hover, native file dialogs, Orca's wizard.\n=== open-file-in-app-without-screen-control\n---\nname: open-file-in-app-without-screen-control\ndescription: \"Drive \\\"open a file\\\" in a scratch copy of the built app with no screen control — AppleScript open addressed to the copy's path works; hidden Home page timers don't run; always override the model endpoint first.\"\nmetadata:\n  node_type: memory\n  type: reference\n  originSessionId: 72fc1a8c-e5fe-483e-9283-9be1cc811037\n  modified: 2026-10-28T15:37:18.379Z\n---\n\n2026-10-28 (phantom edit rows, critique 1B-02): Kenneth declined computer-use control of the app. What worked for \"open a file in the running app\" (the Finder path → `GUI_App::MacOpenFiles` → `ShellController::take_opened_files`):\n\n`osascript -e 'tell application \"<scratch>/App.app\" to open POSIX file \"<file>\"'` — addresses the copy by its bundle path, so it reaches that instance and not another session's `io.jusprin.JusPrin`. It prints \"missing value\" and works. `open -g -a <path> <file>` was unreliable (lsappinfo held stale dead entries for the same path); if you use it, add `--args --datadir <scratch>` so a fresh launch can't touch the real data folder.\n\nDo NOT Finder-open a `.3mf` this way: with `single_instance` off, `MacOpenFiles` calls `start_new_slicer`, a second instance on the default (real) data dir.\n\nThe Home page's injected-script approach ([[live-host-check-via-instrumented-dev-page]]) fails for Home actions while Prepare is showing: the hidden Home web view runs no timers. The Agent page snapshot (`snap` → outerHTML → headless Chrome) still works for screenshots.\n\nOpening a model starts an automatic first agent turn with the saved key. Set `JUSPRIN_AGENT_ENDPOINT=http://127.0.0.1:9/v1` before launching, or a live model call goes out (it did once that day). See [[prompt-eval-spend-budget]].\n\nFor which code path published something, `lldb -b -s cmds` with `breakpoint set -n \"<fully qualified name>\"` + `bt 60` + `continue` works; `-r \"...$\"` regexes resolved to nothing.\n=== drive-app-with-posted-key-events\n---\nname: drive-app-with-posted-key-events\ndescription: \"Drive the built JusPrin app headlessly (even with the screen locked) by posting CGEvents to its pid with a tiny Swift tool; keys work, mouse clicks do not, and the send dialog is reachable by keyboard.\"\nmetadata: \n  node_type: memory\n  type: project\n  originSessionId: 6b96dccc-1cb4-4f72-9de4-3ecee4b28e74\n  modified: 2026-09-08T05:58:16.222Z\n---\n\nWhen the Mac screen is locked (`ioreg -n Root -d1 | grep CGSSessionScreenIsLocked`), the computer-use MCP request is auto-denied, `screencapture` fails, and System Events sees zero windows. Key events still reach the app: a 15-line Swift program calling `CGEvent(keyboardEventSource:virtualKey:keyDown:).postToPid(pid)` (compile with `swiftc`) made the app slice on Cmd+R (keycode 15) and open the send dialog on Cmd+Shift+G (keycode 5). Mouse events posted the same way did nothing, even with the window number set on the event.\n\nInside `PrintHostSendDialog` (Orca `MsgDialog`), focus starts in the filename field; Tab (48) moves to the \"Upload\" button, Right (124) to \"Upload and Print\", Space (49) presses it, because Orca's custom `Button` handles Space/Return and arrow navigation itself. Return alone triggers plain \"Upload\" (the affirmative id), not print.\n\n`CGWindowListCopyWindowInfo` still lists the app's on-screen windows with bounds while locked, which tells you when a modal dialog is open (a small layer-0 window appears) and when it closed.\n\n**Why:** On 2026-09-07 the end-to-end proof of the fake Moonraker printer needed the Print button pressed while the screen was locked; this was the only working path.\n\n**How to apply:** Confirm the target pid first (`pgrep -f <copy>.app/Contents/MacOS`) so keys never go to another session's instance. Watch the app's own `--datadir` `log/debug_*.log` for effects (use `/usr/bin/grep -a`; the default `grep` is ugrep, which treats `\\|` literally and may skip the log as binary). See [[live-test-built-app-on-mac]] and [[fake-moonraker-printer-sim]].","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"1a7024c2-cdce-43b2-88bc-71512e9bb792","timestamp":"2026-11-06T01:39:56.369Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"=== ux-walkthrough-real-app-recipe\n---\nname: ux-walkthrough-real-app-recipe\ndescription: \"How to drive the real built JusPrin app for a screenshot-per-step UX walkthrough (2026-10-28): scratch copies, the empty local_machines loop with the fake printer, why background app_* tools fail on Orca dialogs, and where screenshots land.\"\nmetadata:\n  node_type: memory\n  type: project\n  originSessionId: 33551592-d22c-4161-9a14-9a22ef798541\n  modified: 2026-10-28T13:12:42.393Z\n---\n\nOn 2026-10-28 I walked six scenarios (open-and-print, fix-a-problem) through the real app with Opus 5.5 and published the critique at https://claude.ai/artifact/XyVvteGiKhiJ6apUx8rcmR (34 frames, scratch copy at scratchpad/ux/ of that session). Kenneth's steer: start from files people actually download (MakerWorld 3MFs carry a full Bambu profile: printer, print preset, filaments, colours, bed type, designer, licence), not from generated STLs. `~/Downloads` has Tape_4_3MF.3mf (A1 mini profile), find_my_hollow.3mf (P1S, 3 colours, 233 mm wide, too big for an A1 mini), arrow_headband.3mf (P1S), general_purpose_hook.STL (bare).\n\n**Recipe that worked**\n- `ditto` the built .app out of `build/arm64/src/RelWithDebInfo/` into the scratchpad before launching (another session's ninja can relink it underneath you); the bundle id is already unique (`io.jusprin.JusPrin`), no re-sign needed.\n- `ditto` `~/Library/Application Support/JusPrin2` to a scratch `--datadir`; set `jusprin.fake_printer=true`, `presets.machine` to the saved \"Bambu Lab A1 mini 2\", write `jusprin/fake_printer.json`, delete `jusprin/mcp.json.lock`.\n- **Clear `local_machines`.** Kenneth's conf carries a `local_machines` entry keyed by the empty string (old Moonraker experiment). With the fake Bambu agent on, `init_networking_callbacks`' connect callback calls `DeviceManager::set_selected_machine(\"\")` in a loop (\"same lan machine, dev_id =, disconnect and reconnect\"), the main window disappears and the log grew 700 MB in two minutes. Clearing the map fixed it. The loop has no guard; see [[fake-bambu-printer-sim]] and [[harness-fake-printer-cleanup]].\n- Background `app_*` tools cannot press OrcaSlicer's custom `Button`s (no AX action) and the hit test at the dialog's screen position reports \"belongs to a different process\". `request_full_control` + `computer_batch` works for everything, including the Agent web view and the macOS file chooser (`cmd+shift+g`, type the path, Return, Return). Re-front the app with `open_application` when another session's harness steals focus.\n- Every `app_screenshot`/`computer_batch` screenshot is written as a JPEG under `~/.claude/projects/<project>/<session>/tool-results/mcp-computer-use-blob-*.jpg`; copy those for a report instead of fighting `screencapture`.\n- The dev build (-O0) slices a 38 mm part in over a minute; wait 45–60 s before judging a slice.\n\n**Why:** the first launch attempt looked like an app bug (blank window, title \"Couldn't save\") and cost ten minutes; the dialog-click refusals cost another ten.\n**How to apply:** reuse this for any \"walk through the app as a user\" request; keep scenarios on downloaded files; write the critique per step as what the person knows / sees / finds confusing. Related: [[live-test-built-app-on-mac]], [[drive-app-with-posted-key-events]].\n=== scratch-app-driving-traps\n---\nname: scratch-app-driving-traps\ndescription: \"Five traps met driving a scratch copy of the built app without screen control (2026-11-04): in-place binary copy gets SIGKILL, Home drops bridge messages while hidden, header popups need a posted NSEvent, lldb std::string args, wx Wrap reuse.\"\nmetadata:\n  node_type: memory\n  type: reference\n  originSessionId: dea8379c-b02c-43a2-a254-4c2259672439\n  modified: 2026-11-04T18:59:38.548Z\n---\n\nMet while verifying print-host printer window fixes on the scratch `.app` (see [[live-test-built-app-on-mac]], [[open-file-in-app-without-screen-control]]).\n\n- **Copy a new build into a `.app` with `rm` then `cp`.** `cp` over the existing signed binary keeps the inode; the kernel kills the launch at once (exit 137, nothing logged).\n- **A launch from a plain Bash call dies when the call ends.** Start the app with `run_in_background: true` and `exec`.\n- **Home ignores bridge messages while the main window shows a project.** A queued `launch_monitor` through `JUSPRIN_HOME_DEV_URL` is sent by the page and silently dropped; switch to Home first (`m_tabpanel->SetSelection(0)` via lldb).\n- **Background `app_click` does not reach the header's popup menus** (they are not listed as windows). Post the click into the app's queue with lldb: `expr -l objc -- @import AppKit`, then `NSEvent mouseEventWithType:NSEventTypeLeftMouseDown/Up location:NSMakePoint(x, y-from-popup-bottom) ... windowNumber:[popup windowNumber]` and `[NSApp postEvent:atStart:NO]`. Render the popup with `cacheDisplayInRect:` on its contentView ([[capture-mac-popups-for-platform-diff]]).\n- **lldb cannot build `std::string` args.** This libc++ uses the alternate short-string layout: a 24-byte char array with the text at offset 0 and its length in byte 23 (≤ 22 chars), passed as `*(std::string*)buf`.\n- **wx `wxStaticText::Wrap()` (Orca's wx) skips a width it already wrapped at and keeps the first text it wrapped**, so SetLabel + Wrap on a reused label comes back unwrapped. Use a fresh label.\n=== live-test-built-app-on-mac\n---\nname: live-test-built-app-on-mac\ndescription: \"How to launch, see, and drive the locally built JusPrin app on the Mac: the shared bundle id binds tools to the wrong instance, and \\\"on another Space\\\" usually means the window is on the second monitor, not that the user is in full screen.\"\nmetadata: \n  node_type: memory\n  type: project\n  originSessionId: fa2d66ed-e217-440b-aae0-da4164953edc\n  modified: 2026-11-01T19:29:08.107Z\n---\n\nEvery build of the fork (and /Applications/OrcaSlicer.app) shares bundle id `com.softfever3d.orca-slicer`. The desktop-control tools resolve an app by bundle id and bind to whichever instance comes first, so `app_list_windows` returns `[]` and filtered screenshots hide the window you actually launched.\n\n**Working recipe (2026-09-05):** `ditto` the built .app into the scratchpad, `plutil -replace CFBundleIdentifier -string com.jusprin.worktree-test`, `codesign --force --deep -s -`, then `open -n <copy>.app --args <model>` and `request_access` for the new id. `app_screenshot`/`app_click` then work and include popup menus. A display-scope `left_click` on the header did NOT open the fork's PopupWindow menus, but a background `app_click` did; take the pixel-level `zoom` with the display tools afterwards (call `app_release` first). Display-scope `Escape` does not close those popups; a click elsewhere does.\n\nThe MCP discovery file `~/Library/Application Support/JusPrin2/jusprin/mcp.json` points at the newest instance's `http://127.0.0.1:<port>/mcp`; `tests/mcp/probe.py`'s `call()` can drive real tools (e.g. `workspace_inspect`, then `report_slice_review` with sessionId/plateId/sliceResultId) to put the header into the Check-print state without lldb. lldb `expr` cannot call inline accessors like `status_row()`.\n\n**Why:** On 2026-09-01 a verification pass screenshotted the stock app instead of the build; on 2026-09-05 the tools bound to another session's main-repo build.\n\n**How to apply:** Confirm the pid with `pgrep -fl OrcaSlicer.app/Contents/MacOS`; never kill an instance you did not launch. `osascript` System Events by unix id still works to set `frontmost`. See [[jusprin-shell-phase-1-design]] and [[orca-inherited-teardown-crash]].\n\n**\"On another Space\" usually means \"on the other monitor.\"** Cost about ten turns on\n2026-09-09 and produced a wrong report to Kenneth. `app_list_windows` returns\n`is_off_space: true` and clicks are refused with \"this window is on another Space\";\n`app_bring_to_current_space` then fails with \"the user's current Space is a full-screen\napp.\" Both messages are about Spaces, so the natural read is that the user is sitting in\na full-screen app — but with *Displays have separate Spaces* on, a window merely sitting\non the second monitor produces exactly the same symptoms. Kenneth was not in full screen;\nthe harness had opened on the Acer.\n\nTell them apart before saying anything to the user: take a **display-scope** screenshot\n(`app_release`, then `computer_batch` screenshot). Its header names the monitor it\ncaptured and lists the others — if the window shows up there, it is a monitor problem,\nnot a Space problem, and the display-scope tools can drive it immediately. Never conclude\n\"the user is in a full-screen app\" from the background tools' error text alone.\n\nThe same flag also flaps: a window can read `is_off_space: false` and click fine, then\nread `true` a minute later. Clicks delivered while it is true report `ok ... unverified`\nand silently do nothing. **A click that reports \"unverified\" and changes nothing is not\nevidence of an application bug** — on 2026-09-09 that nearly became a filed defect about\nbeing unable to retry after a failed MCP connect. Re-verify on a reachable window before\nconcluding anything about the app.\n\n**Prefer the shell harness over a re-signed app copy for Agent-panel work.**\n`tests/shell/.../JusPrinShellHarness.app` already carries its own bundle id\n(`io.jusprin.shell-harness`), so none of the bundle-id collision above applies, and\n`--manual-unconfigured` lands directly on the dock's not-set-up state — one click from\nthe Agent setup chooser. Build target is `shell_integration_harness`, not `shell_harness`.\n\n**Isolate `$HOME` when testing MCP client setup.** `Mcp::default_catalog_paths()` reads\n`$HOME`, so the flow will happily rewrite the real `~/.cursor/mcp.json`. Launch with\n`HOME=<scratch>` holding a `.cursor/mcp.json` fixture; detection, the diff, and the write\nall follow it. Force a write failure with `chmod 444` on the file **and** `555` on its\ndirectory — the directory alone is not enough.\n\n**Re-signed copies trigger system prompts.** Each rebuild + ad-hoc re-sign changes the cdhash, so macOS re-asks for Downloads access (recent-project thumbnail load blocks in `fopen`) and Keychain access (agent runtime reads the API key). Both are prompts only the user can answer. Avoid them by running the binary directly (`nohup <copy>.app/Contents/MacOS/OrcaSlicer --datadir <scratch copy of JusPrin2 with recent_projects cleared> <model>`) with `OPENAI_API_KEY=<placeholder>` in the environment, which short-circuits the Keychain lookup in `AgentConfiguration.cpp`. Use `sample <pid>` on the main thread to see which prompt is blocking.\n\n**Stale as of 2026-09-18 (branch claude/printer-conversation-panel-af11cb):** `load_agent_runtime` reads the key only from app config (`jusprin_agent` / `openai_api_key`); no env var or Keychain lookup exists there. In the shell harness, `OPENAI_API_KEY` only feeds the docked pane via `install_harness_agent`; the printer panel builds its own runtime from app config, so `--printer-live` writes the key into the run's throwaway conf. Pass it as `std::string`: `AppConfig::set(section, key, const char*)` silently picks the `bool` overload and stores `true` (seen as a 401 \"key rejected\"). The harness temp data dir then holds the real key: delete `/var/folders/*/*/T/jusprin-shell-*` dirs from those runs afterwards.\n\n**Hands-on printer panel with a live model (2026-09-23, jusprin-newui, uncommitted at the time):** `--manual-live-agent` now also writes `OPENAI_API_KEY` into the run's app config, so Home → \"+ Add printer\" gets a live printer chat. Feed the key from `~/Library/Application Support/JusPrin2/JusPrin2.conf` (`jusprin_agent.openai_api_key`) via env without echoing it. Drive it with display-scope `computer_batch` clicks/typing (background `app_click` does nothing on the web view). The scripted `--printer-live` run hangs when the model doesn't pick the printer its next \"tap\" step expects; kill it. Afterwards `rm -rf` the run's `/var/folders/*/*/T/jusprin-shell-*` dir — killed runs leave it behind with the key.\n\n=== fake-host-page-fixture\n---\nname: fake-host-page-fixture\ndescription: \"Render the built AgentUI/HomeUI bundles in the built-in browser with a scripted fake native host, to see page states the live app makes hard to catch\"\nmetadata: \n  node_type: memory\n  type: reference\n  originSessionId: 9bb21a20-a19f-4500-adcf-139798a1201d\n  modified: 2026-09-19T16:55:23.039Z\n---\n\nBoth pages find their host through `window.wx.postMessage(json)` and receive host\nenvelopes through `window.__jusprinBridge.deliver(envelope)` (`WebShared/bridgeClient.ts`).\nCopy `resources/jusprin/{agent,home}/index.html` to a scratch dir, inject\n`<script>` right after `<head>` that (1) defines `window.wx` answering `hello` with\n`hello_ack` + a full `state`, and (2) exposes `window.fake.deliver(type, payload)`;\nserve with `python3 -m http.server` and open `agent.html?panel=printer` /\n`home.html` via `preview_start`. Drive it with `javascript_tool`: deliver\n`assistant_started` with no `assistant_delta` to freeze a streaming empty turn,\n`printer_session` to pin a card, `printer_added` for Home's receipt strip. A file\ndrop works with `new DragEvent('drop', {dataTransfer})` on `.app--printer`.\nEnvelope: `{protocol:'jusprin-agent-bridge'|'jusprin-home-bridge', version:1, id, type, payload}`.\nUsed 2026-09-19 to review branch these-commits-are-probably-wrong in ~10 minutes.\n\n**Why:** the desktop tools were locked by another session and background\n`app_click` never reaches WKWebView content, so page-level states (streaming\nactivity line, compact photo chip, leave dialog, receipt strip) had no other cheap\nproof. It proves page rendering only; host behaviour (e.g. the 256 KiB image\npreview cap `kInlineImagePreviewCap` in `AgentHost.cpp`) must be replicated in\nthe fake by hand or checked live.\n\n**How to apply:** reach for this before building a full app + datadir copy when the\nquestion is \"what does the page draw for state X\". Pair with [[live-test-built-app-on-mac]]\nfor the host side. Related: [[render-widget-to-bitmap-for-visual-proof]].\n=== screenshots-to-files-via-page-fixture\n---\nname: screenshots-to-files-via-page-fixture\ndescription: \"computer_batch save_to_disk produced no files (2026-09-23); to get screenshot files for a report, replay the observed host state into the built Agent/Home page under Playwright, which saves PNGs; plus the window-overlap trap when another session runs the harness.\"\nmetadata:\n  node_type: memory\n  type: project\n  originSessionId: 49ad3806-419d-49f2-8833-1578cd5bf2b3\n  modified: 2026-09-23T21:16:58.377Z\n---\n\nOn 2026-09-23 a full live walkthrough of the printer panel was driven with display-scope `computer_batch` (`zoom` + `save_to_disk: true`). Every call returned the image, but no path was reported and a disk-wide search found no file. Do not count on `save_to_disk` for deliverables.\n\n**What worked for files:** the [[fake-host-page-fixture]] recipe under the Playwright MCP. Copy `resources/jusprin/agent/index.html` (and `home/index.html`), inject `window.wx` + a `window.SCENES` table of full `state` payloads, serve with `python3 -m http.server`, open `agent.html?panel=printer`, switch scenes with `browser_evaluate` and save with `browser_take_screenshot` (`scale: device`, `filename` under the repo's `.playwright-mcp/`, the only allowed root; move the PNGs out and `rm -rf .playwright-mcp` afterwards so `git status` stays clean). Real printer pictures come from `resources/profiles/<Vendor>/<Model>_cover.png` as data URLs. The credential card renders from a `toolActivities` entry with `tool: 'printer_connect'`, `correlationId` = an assistant message id, state `pending` (card) or `succeeded` (\"Sent\"). Chips come from a trailing `Choices: a | b` line. 13 scenes took about 10 minutes and matched the live rendering.\n\n**Window overlap trap:** when another session runs `JusPrinShellHarness --printer-live` in a loop, each run opens a 1200x800 window at the same origin (360,125) on the primary display and takes the front, so display-scope zooms and clicks land on *its* window. Move your own instance by pid with a 20-line Swift AX helper (`AXUIElementCreateApplication(pid)` → `kAXPositionAttribute`) onto the built-in display (bounds start at y=1080 here), then `switch_display \"Built-in Retina Display\"`. The first display click only focuses the window; click again. `--manual-live-agent` does not enable the fake Bambu printer, so the Bambu connect path is out of reach in manual mode.\n\n**Why:** the walkthrough's evidence would otherwise have been lost, and a click into the other session's scripted run could have corrupted its result.\n\n**How to apply:** for any \"take screenshots\" request on the web pages, plan on the fixture route for files from the start and use the live app only to observe. See [[live-test-built-app-on-mac]] and [[printer-live-harness-lessons]].\n=== real-app-signed-in-without-screen-control\n---\nname: real-app-signed-in-without-screen-control\ndescription: \"Drive the real app signed in to a local gateway through an injected page script; which conf keys, why a copied binary dies, and what still needs the screen.\"\nmetadata:\n  node_type: memory\n  type: reference\n  originSessionId: f57d8b7e-fd5a-4daf-9378-2e3d21342f7c\n  modified: 2026-11-02T13:45:04.141Z\n---\n\nBuilds on [[live-host-check-via-instrumented-dev-page]]; used 2026-11-02 when screen control of the app was denied.\n\n- Signed-in conf needs all of: `jusprin_agent.{provider=jusprin, jusprin_api_key, enabled=true, cloud_consent=true, jusprin_model_formats=<JSON id→format from GET /ent/jusprin/v2/models>}`, `jusprin_server.base_url`, `jusprin_onboarding.status=completed`. Without the formats the Agent says \"not set up\".\n- An installed printer is `\"models\":[{\"vendor\":\"Custom\",\"model\":\"Generic Klipper Printer\",\"nozzle_diameter\":\"0.4\"}]`, not `vendors`.\n- Kill the app before editing the conf. Replace a scratch binary with `rm` then `cp`: `cp` over a binary that has run gets the new process killed at launch.\n- `Contents/Resources` in the build is a symlink to the worktree. Replace it with a real folder of links before corrupting a resource, or the worktree gets corrupted.\n- Bringing the app forward triggers an account refresh, so to race the gateway (a real 402), change the ledger and send without refocusing.\n- Page text input: native value setter plus an `input` event. A modal Preferences window's page polls as `agent-preferences`.\n- A test preset needs a `version` field or import rejects it.\n- A compose recreate drops env set by a wrapper; check `JUSPRIN_MODEL_ALIASES` before any chat so only the fake upstream is reachable.\n\nStill needs the screen: pointer hover, native file dialogs, Orca's wizard.\n=== open-file-in-app-without-screen-control\n---\nname: open-file-in-app-without-screen-control\ndescription: \"Drive \\\"open a file\\\" in a scratch copy of the built app with no screen control — AppleScript open addressed to the copy's path works; hidden Home page timers don't run; always override the model endpoint first.\"\nmetadata:\n  node_type: memory\n  type: reference\n  originSessionId: 72fc1a8c-e5fe-483e-9283-9be1cc811037\n  modified: 2026-10-28T15:37:18.379Z\n---\n\n2026-10-28 (phantom edit rows, critique 1B-02): Kenneth declined computer-use control of the app. What worked for \"open a file in the running app\" (the Finder path → `GUI_App::MacOpenFiles` → `ShellController::take_opened_files`):\n\n`osascript -e 'tell application \"<scratch>/App.app\" to open POSIX file \"<file>\"'` — addresses the copy by its bundle path, so it reaches that instance and not another session's `io.jusprin.JusPrin`. It prints \"missing value\" and works. `open -g -a <path> <file>` was unreliable (lsappinfo held stale dead entries for the same path); if you use it, add `--args --datadir <scratch>` so a fresh launch can't touch the real data folder.\n\nDo NOT Finder-open a `.3mf` this way: with `single_instance` off, `MacOpenFiles` calls `start_new_slicer`, a second instance on the default (real) data dir.\n\nThe Home page's injected-script approach ([[live-host-check-via-instrumented-dev-page]]) fails for Home actions while Prepare is showing: the hidden Home web view runs no timers. The Agent page snapshot (`snap` → outerHTML → headless Chrome) still works for screenshots.\n\nOpening a model starts an automatic first agent turn with the saved key. Set `JUSPRIN_AGENT_ENDPOINT=http://127.0.0.1:9/v1` before launching, or a live model call goes out (it did once that day). See [[prompt-eval-spend-budget]].\n\nFor which code path published something, `lldb -b -s cmds` with `breakpoint set -n \"<fully qualified name>\"` + `bt 60` + `continue` works; `-r \"...$\"` regexes resolved to nothing.\n=== drive-app-with-posted-key-events\n---\nname: drive-app-with-posted-key-events\ndescription: \"Drive the built JusPrin app headlessly (even with the screen locked) by posting CGEvents to its pid with a tiny Swift tool; keys work, mouse clicks do not, and the send dialog is reachable by keyboard.\"\nmetadata: \n  node_type: memory\n  type: project\n  originSessionId: 6b96dccc-1cb4-4f72-9de4-3ecee4b28e74\n  modified: 2026-09-08T05:58:16.222Z\n---\n\nWhen the Mac screen is locked (`ioreg -n Root -d1 | grep CGSSessionScreenIsLocked`), the computer-use MCP request is auto-denied, `screencapture` fails, and System Events sees zero windows. Key events still reach the app: a 15-line Swift program calling `CGEvent(keyboardEventSource:virtualKey:keyDown:).postToPid(pid)` (compile with `swiftc`) made the app slice on Cmd+R (keycode 15) and open the send dialog on Cmd+Shift+G (keycode 5). Mouse events posted the same way did nothing, even with the window number set on the event.\n\nInside `PrintHostSendDialog` (Orca `MsgDialog`), focus starts in the filename field; Tab (48) moves to the \"Upload\" button, Right (124) to \"Upload and Print\", Space (49) presses it, because Orca's custom `Button` handles Space/Return and arrow navigation itself. Return alone triggers plain \"Upload\" (the affirmative id), not print.\n\n`CGWindowListCopyWindowInfo` still lists the app's on-screen windows with bounds while locked, which tells you when a modal dialog is open (a small layer-0 window appears) and when it closed.\n\n**Why:** On 2026-09-07 the end-to-end proof of the fake Moonraker printer needed the Print button pressed while the screen was locked; this was the only working path.\n\n**How to apply:** Confirm the target pid first (`pgrep -f <copy>.app/Contents/MacOS`) so keys never go to another session's instance. Watch the app's own `--datadir` `log/debug_*.log` for effects (use `/usr/bin/grep -a`; the default `grep` is ugrep, which treats `\\|` literally and may skip the log as binary). See [[live-test-built-app-on-mac]] and [[fake-moonraker-printer-sim]].","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"458dd890-02fe-4e4d-a92e-9475a062dc26","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/.claude/projects/-Users-kenneth-Projects-JusPrin/figma-mirror","sessionId":"473348c5-5f94-4e4d-9ad9-c7e9dd10b438","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"jusprin-newui","slug":"glimmering-doodling-lovelace"}
{"parentUuid":"1a7024c2-cdce-43b2-88bc-71512e9bb792","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"output_style","style":"Plain"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"34414646-be6b-453b-bab4-a225b944189a","timestamp":"2026-11-06T01:39:56.378Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nPlain output style is active. Remember to follow the specific guidelines for this style.\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/.claude/projects/-Users-kenneth-Projects-JusPrin/figma-mirror","sessionId":"473348c5-5f94-4e4d-9ad9-c7e9dd10b438","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"jusprin-newui","slug":"glimmering-doodling-lovelace"}
{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"473348c5-5f94-4e4d-9ad9-c7e9dd10b438","hash":"2920e6c40fc81bd4a85e647550e3a1e342f5ffe7aeed2411179d8e6b2a5ba72c","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01LgnXv99QkJAEvDYi1vMcib","name":"mcp__ccd_turn__update_plan","input":{"items":[{"content":"Read the walkthrough recipes and find the current build","status":"in_progress"},{"content":"Set up a scratch app and data folder","status":"pending"},{"content":"Walk every first-run path and capture screens","status":"pending"},{"content":"Review sign-in, credits and printer wording against the boards","status":"pending"},{"content":"Write the report with screenshots","status":"pending"}],"scope":"continuation"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01HtLHVdY7i77NoWHpH7jRBz","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"D=/Users/kenneth/.claude/projects/-Users-kenneth-Projects-JusPrin/memory; for f in ux-walkthrough-real-app-recipe scratch-app-driving-traps live-test-built-app-on-mac fake-host-page-fixture screenshots-to-files-via-page-fixture real-app-signed-in-without-screen-control open-file-in-app-without-screen-control drive-app-with-posted-key-events; do echo \"=== $f\"; cat $D/$f.md | sed -n 1,60p; done"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"473348c5-5f94-4e4d-9ad9-c7e9dd10b438","hash":"9bb794e073d8fc05ae615f1fac9277567f7018423e5d6bbb9faac62110b3ded6","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LgnXv99QkJAEvDYi1vMcib","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Plan shown (5 steps)."}]},{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HtLHVdY7i77NoWHpH7jRBz","type":"tool_result","content":"=== ux-walkthrough-real-app-recipe\n---\nname: ux-walkthrough-real-app-recipe\ndescription: \"How to drive the real built JusPrin app for a screenshot-per-step UX walkthrough (2026-10-28): scratch copies, the empty local_machines loop with the fake printer, why background app_* tools fail on Orca dialogs, and where screenshots land.\"\nmetadata:\n  node_type: memory\n  type: project\n  originSessionId: 33551592-d22c-4161-9a14-9a22ef798541\n  modified: 2026-10-28T13:12:42.393Z\n---\n\nOn 2026-10-28 I walked six scenarios (open-and-print, fix-a-problem) through the real app with Opus 5.5 and published the critique at https://claude.ai/artifact/XyVvteGiKhiJ6apUx8rcmR (34 frames, scratch copy at scratchpad/ux/ of that session). Kenneth's steer: start from files people actually download (MakerWorld 3MFs carry a full Bambu profile: printer, print preset, filaments, colours, bed type, designer, licence), not from generated STLs. `~/Downloads` has Tape_4_3MF.3mf (A1 mini profile), find_my_hollow.3mf (P1S, 3 colours, 233 mm wide, too big for an A1 mini), arrow_headband.3mf (P1S), general_purpose_hook.STL (bare).\n\n**Recipe that worked**\n- `ditto` the built .app out of `build/arm64/src/RelWithDebInfo/` into the scratchpad before launching (another session's ninja can relink it underneath you); the bundle id is already unique (`io.jusprin.JusPrin`), no re-sign needed.\n- `ditto` `~/Library/Application Support/JusPrin2` to a scratch `--datadir`; set `jusprin.fake_printer=true`, `presets.machine` to the saved \"Bambu Lab A1 mini 2\", write `jusprin/fake_printer.json`, delete `jusprin/mcp.json.lock`.\n- **Clear `local_machines`.** Kenneth's conf carries a `local_machines` entry keyed by the empty string (old Moonraker experiment). With the fake Bambu agent on, `init_networking_callbacks`' connect callback calls `DeviceManager::set_selected_machine(\"\")` in a loop (\"same lan machine, dev_id =, disconnect and reconnect\"), the main window disappears and the log grew 700 MB in two minutes. Clearing the map fixed it. The loop has no guard; see [[fake-bambu-printer-sim]] and [[harness-fake-printer-cleanup]].\n- Background `app_*` tools cannot press OrcaSlicer's custom `Button`s (no AX action) and the hit test at the dialog's screen position reports \"belongs to a different process\". `request_full_control` + `computer_batch` works for everything, including the Agent web view and the macOS file chooser (`cmd+shift+g`, type the path, Return, Return). Re-front the app with `open_application` when another session's harness steals focus.\n- Every `app_screenshot`/`computer_batch` screenshot is written as a JPEG under `~/.claude/projects/<project>/<session>/tool-results/mcp-computer-use-blob-*.jpg`; copy those for a report instead of fighting `screencapture`.\n- The dev build (-O0) slices a 38 mm part in over a minute; wait 45–60 s before judging a slice.\n\n**Why:** the first launch attempt looked like an app bug (blank window, title \"Couldn't save\") and cost ten minutes; the dialog-click refusals cost another ten.\n**How to apply:** reuse this for any \"walk through the app as a user\" request; keep scenarios on downloaded files; write the critique per step as what the person knows / sees / finds confusing. Related: [[live-test-built-app-on-mac]], [[drive-app-with-posted-key-events]].\n=== scratch-app-driving-traps\n---\nname: scratch-app-driving-traps\ndescription: \"Five traps met driving a scratch copy of the built app without screen control (2026-11-04): in-place binary copy gets SIGKILL, Home drops bridge messages while hidden, header popups need a posted NSEvent, lldb std::string args, wx Wrap reuse.\"\nmetadata:\n  node_type: memory\n  type: reference\n  originSessionId: dea8379c-b02c-43a2-a254-4c2259672439\n  modified: 2026-11-04T18:59:38.548Z\n---\n\nMet while verifying print-host printer window fixes on the scratch `.app` (see [[live-test-built-app-on-mac]], [[open-file-in-app-without-screen-control]]).\n\n- **Copy a new build into a `.app` with `rm` then `cp`.** `cp` over the existing signed binary keeps the inode; the kernel kills the launch at once (exit 137, nothing logged).\n- **A launch from a plain Bash call dies when the call ends.** Start the app with `run_in_background: true` and `exec`.\n- **Home ignores bridge messages while the main window shows a project.** A queued `launch_monitor` through `JUSPRIN_HOME_DEV_URL` is sent by the page and silently dropped; switch to Home first (`m_tabpanel->SetSelection(0)` via lldb).\n- **Background `app_click` does not reach the header's popup menus** (they are not listed as windows). Post the click into the app's queue with lldb: `expr -l objc -- @import AppKit`, then `NSEvent mouseEventWithType:NSEventTypeLeftMouseDown/Up location:NSMakePoint(x, y-from-popup-bottom) ... windowNumber:[popup windowNumber]` and `[NSApp postEvent:atStart:NO]`. Render the popup with `cacheDisplayInRect:` on its contentView ([[capture-mac-popups-for-platform-diff]]).\n- **lldb cannot build `std::string` args.** This libc++ uses the alternate short-string layout: a 24-byte char array with the text at offset 0 and its length in byte 23 (≤ 22 chars), passed as `*(std::string*)buf`.\n- **wx `wxStaticText::Wrap()` (Orca's wx) skips a width it already wrapped at and keeps the first text it wrapped**, so SetLabel + Wrap on a reused label comes back unwrapped. Use a fresh label.\n=== live-test-built-app-on-mac\n---\nname: live-test-built-app-on-mac\ndescription: \"How to launch, see, and drive the locally built JusPrin app on the Mac: the shared bundle id binds tools to the wrong instance, and \\\"on another Space\\\" usually means the window is on the second monitor, not that the user is in full screen.\"\nmetadata: \n  node_type: memory\n  type: project\n  originSessionId: fa2d66ed-e217-440b-aae0-da4164953edc\n  modified: 2026-11-01T19:29:08.107Z\n---\n\nEvery build of the fork (and /Applications/OrcaSlicer.app) shares bundle id `com.softfever3d.orca-slicer`. The desktop-control tools resolve an app by bundle id and bind to whichever instance comes first, so `app_list_windows` returns `[]` and filtered screenshots hide the window you actually launched.\n\n**Working recipe (2026-09-05):** `ditto` the built .app into the scratchpad, `plutil -replace CFBundleIdentifier -string com.jusprin.worktree-test`, `codesign --force --deep -s -`, then `open -n <copy>.app --args <model>` and `request_access` for the new id. `app_screenshot`/`app_click` then work and include popup menus. A display-scope `left_click` on the header did NOT open the fork's PopupWindow menus, but a background `app_click` did; take the pixel-level `zoom` with the display tools afterwards (call `app_release` first). Display-scope `Escape` does not close those popups; a click elsewhere does.\n\nThe MCP discovery file `~/Library/Application Support/JusPrin2/jusprin/mcp.json` points at the newest instance's `http://127.0.0.1:<port>/mcp`; `tests/mcp/probe.py`'s `call()` can drive real tools (e.g. `workspace_inspect`, then `report_slice_review` with sessionId/plateId/sliceResultId) to put the header into the Check-print state without lldb. lldb `expr` cannot call inline accessors like `status_row()`.\n\n**Why:** On 2026-09-01 a verification pass screenshotted the stock app instead of the build; on 2026-09-05 the tools bound to another session's main-repo build.\n\n**How to apply:** Confirm the pid with `pgrep -fl OrcaSlicer.app/Contents/MacOS`; never kill an instance you did not launch. `osascript` System Events by unix id still works to set `frontmost`. See [[jusprin-shell-phase-1-design]] and [[orca-inherited-teardown-crash]].\n\n**\"On another Space\" usually means \"on the other monitor.\"** Cost about ten turns on\n2026-09-09 and produced a wrong report to Kenneth. `app_list_windows` returns\n`is_off_space: true` and clicks are refused with \"this window is on another Space\";\n`app_bring_to_current_space` then fails with \"the user's current Space is a full-screen\napp.\" Both messages are about Spaces, so the natural read is that the user is sitting in\na full-screen app — but with *Displays have separate Spaces* on, a window merely sitting\non the second monitor produces exactly the same symptoms. Kenneth was not in full screen;\nthe harness had opened on the Acer.\n\nTell them apart before saying anything to the user: take a **display-scope** screenshot\n(`app_release`, then `computer_batch` screenshot). Its header names the monitor it\ncaptured and lists the others — if the window shows up there, it is a monitor problem,\nnot a Space problem, and the display-scope tools can drive it immediately. Never conclude\n\"the user is in a full-screen app\" from the background tools' error text alone.\n\nThe same flag also flaps: a window can read `is_off_space: false` and click fine, then\nread `true` a minute later. Clicks delivered while it is true report `ok ... unverified`\nand silently do nothing. **A click that reports \"unverified\" and changes nothing is not\nevidence of an application bug** — on 2026-09-09 that nearly became a filed defect about\nbeing unable to retry after a failed MCP connect. Re-verify on a reachable window before\nconcluding anything about the app.\n\n**Prefer the shell harness over a re-signed app copy for Agent-panel work.**\n`tests/shell/.../JusPrinShellHarness.app` already carries its own bundle id\n(`io.jusprin.shell-harness`), so none of the bundle-id collision above applies, and\n`--manual-unconfigured` lands directly on the dock's not-set-up state — one click from\nthe Agent setup chooser. Build target is `shell_integration_harness`, not `shell_harness`.\n\n**Isolate `$HOME` when testing MCP client setup.** `Mcp::default_catalog_paths()` reads\n`$HOME`, so the flow will happily rewrite the real `~/.cursor/mcp.json`. Launch with\n`HOME=<scratch>` holding a `.cursor/mcp.json` fixture; detection, the diff, and the write\nall follow it. Force a write failure with `chmod 444` on the file **and** `555` on its\ndirectory — the directory alone is not enough.\n\n**Re-signed copies trigger system prompts.** Each rebuild + ad-hoc re-sign changes the cdhash, so macOS re-asks for Downloads access (recent-project thumbnail load blocks in `fopen`) and Keychain access (agent runtime reads the API key). Both are prompts only the user can answer. Avoid them by running the binary directly (`nohup <copy>.app/Contents/MacOS/OrcaSlicer --datadir <scratch copy of JusPrin2 with recent_projects cleared> <model>`) with `OPENAI_API_KEY=<placeholder>` in the environment, which short-circuits the Keychain lookup in `AgentConfiguration.cpp`. Use `sample <pid>` on the main thread to see which prompt is blocking.\n\n**Stale as of 2026-09-18 (branch claude/printer-conversation-panel-af11cb):** `load_agent_runtime` reads the key only from app config (`jusprin_agent` / `openai_api_key`); no env var or Keychain lookup exists there. In the shell harness, `OPENAI_API_KEY` only feeds the docked pane via `install_harness_agent`; the printer panel builds its own runtime from app config, so `--printer-live` writes the key into the run's throwaway conf. Pass it as `std::string`: `AppConfig::set(section, key, const char*)` silently picks the `bool` overload and stores `true` (seen as a 401 \"key rejected\"). The harness temp data dir then holds the real key: delete `/var/folders/*/*/T/jusprin-shell-*` dirs from those runs afterwards.\n\n**Hands-on printer panel with a live model (2026-09-23, jusprin-newui, uncommitted at the time):** `--manual-live-agent` now also writes `OPENAI_API_KEY` into the run's app config, so Home → \"+ Add printer\" gets a live printer chat. Feed the key from `~/Library/Application Support/JusPrin2/JusPrin2.conf` (`jusprin_agent.openai_api_key`) via env without echoing it. Drive it with display-scope `computer_batch` clicks/typing (background `app_click` does nothing on the web view). The scripted `--printer-live` run hangs when the model doesn't pick the printer its next \"tap\" step expects; kill it. Afterwards `rm -rf` the run's `/var/folders/*/*/T/jusprin-shell-*` dir — killed runs leave it behind with the key.\n\n=== fake-host-page-fixture\n---\nname: fake-host-page-fixture\ndescription: \"Render the built AgentUI/HomeUI bundles in the built-in browser with a scripted fake native host, to see page states the live app makes hard to catch\"\nmetadata: \n  node_type: memory\n  type: reference\n  originSessionId: 9bb21a20-a19f-4500-adcf-139798a1201d\n  modified: 2026-09-19T16:55:23.039Z\n---\n\nBoth pages find their host through `window.wx.postMessage(json)` and receive host\nenvelopes through `window.__jusprinBridge.deliver(envelope)` (`WebShared/bridgeClient.ts`).\nCopy `resources/jusprin/{agent,home}/index.html` to a scratch dir, inject\n`<script>` right after `<head>` that (1) defines `window.wx` answering `hello` with\n`hello_ack` + a full `state`, and (2) exposes `window.fake.deliver(type, payload)`;\nserve with `python3 -m http.server` and open `agent.html?panel=printer` /\n`home.html` via `preview_start`. Drive it with `javascript_tool`: deliver\n`assistant_started` with no `assistant_delta` to freeze a streaming empty turn,\n`printer_session` to pin a card, `printer_added` for Home's receipt strip. A file\ndrop works with `new DragEvent('drop', {dataTransfer})` on `.app--printer`.\nEnvelope: `{protocol:'jusprin-agent-bridge'|'jusprin-home-bridge', version:1, id, type, payload}`.\nUsed 2026-09-19 to review branch these-commits-are-probably-wrong in ~10 minutes.\n\n**Why:** the desktop tools were locked by another session and background\n`app_click` never reaches WKWebView content, so page-level states (streaming\nactivity line, compact photo chip, leave dialog, receipt strip) had no other cheap\nproof. It proves page rendering only; host behaviour (e.g. the 256 KiB image\npreview cap `kInlineImagePreviewCap` in `AgentHost.cpp`) must be replicated in\nthe fake by hand or checked live.\n\n**How to apply:** reach for this before building a full app + datadir copy when the\nquestion is \"what does the page draw for state X\". Pair with [[live-test-built-app-on-mac]]\nfor the host side. Related: [[render-widget-to-bitmap-for-visual-proof]].\n=== screenshots-to-files-via-page-fixture\n---\nname: screenshots-to-files-via-page-fixture\ndescription: \"computer_batch save_to_disk produced no files (2026-09-23); to get screenshot files for a report, replay the observed host state into the built Agent/Home page under Playwright, which saves PNGs; plus the window-overlap trap when another session runs the harness.\"\nmetadata:\n  node_type: memory\n  type: project\n  originSessionId: 49ad3806-419d-49f2-8833-1578cd5bf2b3\n  modified: 2026-09-23T21:16:58.377Z\n---\n\nOn 2026-09-23 a full live walkthrough of the printer panel was driven with display-scope `computer_batch` (`zoom` + `save_to_disk: true`). Every call returned the image, but no path was reported and a disk-wide search found no file. Do not count on `save_to_disk` for deliverables.\n\n**What worked for files:** the [[fake-host-page-fixture]] recipe under the Playwright MCP. Copy `resources/jusprin/agent/index.html` (and `home/index.html`), inject `window.wx` + a `window.SCENES` table of full `state` payloads, serve with `python3 -m http.server`, open `agent.html?panel=printer`, switch scenes with `browser_evaluate` and save with `browser_take_screenshot` (`scale: device`, `filename` under the repo's `.playwright-mcp/`, the only allowed root; move the PNGs out and `rm -rf .playwright-mcp` afterwards so `git status` stays clean). Real printer pictures come from `resources/profiles/<Vendor>/<Model>_cover.png` as data URLs. The credential card renders from a `toolActivities` entry with `tool: 'printer_connect'`, `correlationId` = an assistant message id, state `pending` (card) or `succeeded` (\"Sent\"). Chips come from a trailing `Choices: a | b` line. 13 scenes took about 10 minutes and matched the live rendering.\n\n**Window overlap trap:** when another session runs `JusPrinShellHarness --printer-live` in a loop, each run opens a 1200x800 window at the same origin (360,125) on the primary display and takes the front, so display-scope zooms and clicks land on *its* window. Move your own instance by pid with a 20-line Swift AX helper (`AXUIElementCreateApplication(pid)` → `kAXPositionAttribute`) onto the built-in display (bounds start at y=1080 here), then `switch_display \"Built-in Retina Display\"`. The first display click only focuses the window; click again. `--manual-live-agent` does not enable the fake Bambu printer, so the Bambu connect path is out of reach in manual mode.\n\n**Why:** the walkthrough's evidence would otherwise have been lost, and a click into the other session's scripted run could have corrupted its result.\n\n**How to apply:** for any \"take screenshots\" request on the web pages, plan on the fixture route for files from the start and use the live app only to observe. See [[live-test-built-app-on-mac]] and [[printer-live-harness-lessons]].\n=== real-app-signed-in-without-screen-control\n---\nname: real-app-signed-in-without-screen-control\ndescription: \"Drive the real app signed in to a local gateway through an injected page script; which conf keys, why a copied binary dies, and what still needs the screen.\"\nmetadata:\n  node_type: memory\n  type: reference\n  originSessionId: f57d8b7e-fd5a-4daf-9378-2e3d21342f7c\n  modified: 2026-11-02T13:45:04.141Z\n---\n\nBuilds on [[live-host-check-via-instrumented-dev-page]]; used 2026-11-02 when screen control of the app was denied.\n\n- Signed-in conf needs all of: `jusprin_agent.{provider=jusprin, jusprin_api_key, enabled=true, cloud_consent=true, jusprin_model_formats=<JSON id→format from GET /ent/jusprin/v2/models>}`, `jusprin_server.base_url`, `jusprin_onboarding.status=completed`. Without the formats the Agent says \"not set up\".\n- An installed printer is `\"models\":[{\"vendor\":\"Custom\",\"model\":\"Generic Klipper Printer\",\"nozzle_diameter\":\"0.4\"}]`, not `vendors`.\n- Kill the app before editing the conf. Replace a scratch binary with `rm` then `cp`: `cp` over a binary that has run gets the new process killed at launch.\n- `Contents/Resources` in the build is a symlink to the worktree. Replace it with a real folder of links before corrupting a resource, or the worktree gets corrupted.\n- Bringing the app forward triggers an account refresh, so to race the gateway (a real 402), change the ledger and send without refocusing.\n- Page text input: native value setter plus an `input` event. A modal Preferences window's page polls as `agent-preferences`.\n- A test preset needs a `version` field or import rejects it.\n- A compose recreate drops env set by a wrapper; check `JUSPRIN_MODEL_ALIASES` before any chat so only the fake upstream is reachable.\n\nStill needs the screen: pointer hover, native file dialogs, Orca's wizard.\n=== open-file-in-app-without-screen-control\n---\nname: open-file-in-app-without-screen-control\ndescription: \"Drive \\\"open a file\\\" in a scratch copy of the built app with no screen control — AppleScript open addressed to the copy's path works; hidden Home page timers don't run; always override the model endpoint first.\"\nmetadata:\n  node_type: memory\n  type: reference\n  originSessionId: 72fc1a8c-e5fe-483e-9283-9be1cc811037\n  modified: 2026-10-28T15:37:18.379Z\n---\n\n2026-10-28 (phantom edit rows, critique 1B-02): Kenneth declined computer-use control of the app. What worked for \"open a file in the running app\" (the Finder path → `GUI_App::MacOpenFiles` → `ShellController::take_opened_files`):\n\n`osascript -e 'tell application \"<scratch>/App.app\" to open POSIX file \"<file>\"'` — addresses the copy by its bundle path, so it reaches that instance and not another session's `io.jusprin.JusPrin`. It prints \"missing value\" and works. `open -g -a <path> <file>` was unreliable (lsappinfo held stale dead entries for the same path); if you use it, add `--args --datadir <scratch>` so a fresh launch can't touch the real data folder.\n\nDo NOT Finder-open a `.3mf` this way: with `single_instance` off, `MacOpenFiles` calls `start_new_slicer`, a second instance on the default (real) data dir.\n\nThe Home page's injected-script approach ([[live-host-check-via-instrumented-dev-page]]) fails for Home actions while Prepare is showing: the hidden Home web view runs no timers. The Agent page snapshot (`snap` → outerHTML → headless Chrome) still works for screenshots.\n\nOpening a model starts an automatic first agent turn with the saved key. Set `JUSPRIN_AGENT_ENDPOINT=http://127.0.0.1:9/v1` before launching, or a live model call goes out (it did once that day). See [[prompt-eval-spend-budget]].\n\nFor which code path published something, `lldb -b -s cmds` with `breakpoint set -n \"<fully qualified name>\"` + `bt 60` + `continue` works; `-r \"...$\"` regexes resolved to nothing.\n=== drive-app-with-posted-key-events\n---\nname: drive-app-with-posted-key-events\ndescription: \"Drive the built JusPrin app headlessly (even with the screen locked) by posting CGEvents to its pid with a tiny Swift tool; keys work, mouse clicks do not, and the send dialog is reachable by keyboard.\"\nmetadata: \n  node_type: memory\n  type: project\n  originSessionId: 6b96dccc-1cb4-4f72-9de4-3ecee4b28e74\n  modified: 2026-09-08T05:58:16.222Z\n---\n\nWhen the Mac screen is locked (`ioreg -n Root -d1 | grep CGSSessionScreenIsLocked`), the computer-use MCP request is auto-denied, `screencapture` fails, and System Events sees zero windows. Key events still reach the app: a 15-line Swift program calling `CGEvent(keyboardEventSource:virtualKey:keyDown:).postToPid(pid)` (compile with `swiftc`) made the app slice on Cmd+R (keycode 15) and open the send dialog on Cmd+Shift+G (keycode 5). Mouse events posted the same way did nothing, even with the window number set on the event.\n\nInside `PrintHostSendDialog` (Orca `MsgDialog`), focus starts in the filename field; Tab (48) moves to the \"Upload\" button, Right (124) to \"Upload and Print\", Space (49) presses it, because Orca's custom `Button` handles Space/Return and arrow navigation itself. Return alone triggers plain \"Upload\" (the affirmative id), not print.\n\n`CGWindowListCopyWindowInfo` still lists the app's on-screen windows with bounds while locked, which tells you when a modal dialog is open (a small layer-0 window appears) and when it closed.\n\n**Why:** On 2026-09-07 the end-to-end proof of the fake Moonraker printer needed the Print button pressed while the screen was locked; this was the only working path.\n\n**How to apply:** Confirm the target pid first (`pgrep -f <copy>.app/Contents/MacOS`) so keys never go to another session's instance. Watch the app's own `--datadir` `log/debug_*.log` for effects (use `/usr/bin/grep -a`; the default `grep` is ugrep, which treats `\\|` literally and may skip the log as binary). See [[live-test-built-app-on-mac]] and [[fake-moonraker-printer-sim]].","is_error":false}]}}
