:"high","perTurnEffort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/.claude/worktrees/first-run-flow-f7be35","sessionId":"473348c5-5f94-4e4d-9ad9-c7e9dd10b438","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"jusprin-newui","slug":"glimmering-doodling-lovelace"}
{"parentUuid":"586f272b-2b63-41de-886f-96f890587bea","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"ecb09a06-cb84-4541-b46c-4a925331f135","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01V3W5cQ9Y2ZhG44DGKH4eL7","type":"tool_result","content":"(eval):1: no matches found: /private/tmp/claude/claude-502/-Users-kenneth-Projects-JusPrin/*/scratchpad/drive\n---\nname: live-host-check-via-instrumented-dev-page\ndescription: Test host behaviour in the real built app without screen control — point JUSPRIN_AGENT_DEV_URL at a copy of the built page with an injected script that logs envelopes to a local http.server and posts messages itself.\nmetadata:\n  node_type: memory\n  type: reference\n  originSessionId: 59133fd8-af56-4958-bb71-9b4812c085b8\n  modified: 2026-10-21T14:27:05.386Z\n---\n\n2026-10-21 (saved-key work, branch claude/api-key-saved-state): Kenneth declined computer-use control of the app, and the Remove path's AppConfig code only runs in the real app. What worked in ~2 minutes:\n\n1. Copy `resources/jusprin/agent/index.html` to a scratch dir, inject a `<script>` right after `<head>` that polls for `window.__jusprinBridge`, wraps its `deliver` to `fetch('http://127.0.0.1:<port>/log?'+JSON)` the envelopes of interest, and sends page messages with `window.wx.postMessage(JSON.stringify({protocol:'jusprin-agent-bridge',version:1,id,type,payload}))`.\n2. Serve the dir with `python3 -m http.server <port> --bind 127.0.0.1 > server.log`; the request log is the test output.\n3. Launch the built binary directly: `JUSPRIN_AGENT_DEV_URL=http://127.0.0.1:<port>/page.html JUSPRIN_AGENT_ENDPOINT=http://127.0.0.1:9/v1 <app>/Contents/MacOS/OrcaSlicer --datadir <scratch copy of JusPrin2 with real *_api_key items deleted and TESTONLY keys added>`. The endpoint override keeps model-list and chat traffic off the real providers.\n4. Read the data dir's JusPrin2.conf afterwards for persisted effects; delete the scratch data dir.\n\nThe fork's app bundle id is `io.jusprin.JusPrin` (not com.softfever3d.orca-slicer as [[live-test-built-app-on-mac]] says). Related: [[fake-host-page-fixture]] (page-only states), [[jusprin-worktree-build]].\n\n**Screenshots without screen control (2026-10-21):** add a `snap` command that POSTs `document.documentElement.outerHTML` (mark `document.activeElement` with `data-visual-focus` first) to a tiny local receiver, then strip `<script>`s, replace `:focus-visible` with `[data-visual-focus]`, pin `html,body` to the captured width (headless Chrome has a minimum window width) and screenshot. Keep the page running: the web view's timers stop ~10 s after the window loses visibility, so front the app by pid with `osascript … set frontmost` before every step and run `caffeinate -u -d -t 600`. The app follows the macOS appearance, not `dark_color_mode`; for dark captures deliver an `appearance: dark` envelope to the page and reapply it after any full `state` (a chat turn resends it). A stand-in provider (`JUSPRIN_AGENT_ENDPOINT` → local server that hangs while a flag file exists, else answers 401) produces \"checking\" and \"rejected\" for real.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"4a6be8f7-f706-41f0-8df6-2054d28f5bf7","timestamp":"2026-11-06T01:46:11.116Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"(eval):1: no matches found: /private/tmp/claude/claude-502/-Users-kenneth-Projects-JusPrin/*/scratchpad/drive\n---\nname: live-host-check-via-instrumented-dev-page\ndescription: Test host behaviour in the real built app without screen control — point JUSPRIN_AGENT_DEV_URL at a copy of the built page with an injected script that logs envelopes to a local http.server and posts messages itself.\nmetadata:\n  node_type: memory\n  type: reference\n  originSessionId: 59133fd8-af56-4958-bb71-9b4812c085b8\n  modified: 2026-10-21T14:27:05.386Z\n---\n\n2026-10-21 (saved-key work, branch claude/api-key-saved-state): Kenneth declined computer-use control of the app, and the Remove path's AppConfig code only runs in the real app. What worked in ~2 minutes:\n\n1. Copy `resources/jusprin/agent/index.html` to a scratch dir, inject a `<script>` right after `<head>` that polls for `window.__jusprinBridge`, wraps its `deliver` to `fetch('http://127.0.0.1:<port>/log?'+JSON)` the envelopes of interest, and sends page messages with `window.wx.postMessage(JSON.stringify({protocol:'jusprin-agent-bridge',version:1,id,type,payload}))`.\n2. Serve the dir with `python3 -m http.server <port> --bind 127.0.0.1 > server.log`; the request log is the test output.\n3. Launch the built binary directly: `JUSPRIN_AGENT_DEV_URL=http://127.0.0.1:<port>/page.html JUSPRIN_AGENT_ENDPOINT=http://127.0.0.1:9/v1 <app>/Contents/MacOS/OrcaSlicer --datadir <scratch copy of JusPrin2 with real *_api_key items deleted and TESTONLY keys added>`. The endpoint override keeps model-list and chat traffic off the real providers.\n4. Read the data dir's JusPrin2.conf afterwards for persisted effects; delete the scratch data dir.\n\nThe fork's app bundle id is `io.jusprin.JusPrin` (not com.softfever3d.orca-slicer as [[live-test-built-app-on-mac]] says). Related: [[fake-host-page-fixture]] (page-only states), [[jusprin-worktree-build]].\n\n**Screenshots without screen control (2026-10-21):** add a `snap` command that POSTs `document.documentElement.outerHTML` (mark `document.activeElement` with `data-visual-focus` first) to a tiny local receiver, then strip `<script>`s, replace `:focus-visible` with `[data-visual-focus]`, pin `html,body` to the captured width (headless Chrome has a minimum window width) and screenshot. Keep the page running: the web view's timers stop ~10 s after the window loses visibility, so front the app by pid with `osascript … set frontmost` before every step and run `caffeinate -u -d -t 600`. The app follows the macOS appearance, not `dark_color_mode`; for dark captures deliver an `appearance: dark` envelope to the page and reapply it after any full `state` (a chat turn resends it). A stand-in provider (`JUSPRIN_AGENT_ENDPOINT` → local server that hangs while a flag file exists, else answers 401) produces \"checking\" and \"rejected\" for real.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"586f272b-2b63-41de-886f-96f890587bea","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/.claude/worktrees/first-run-flow-f7be35","sessionId":"473348c5-5f94-4e4d-9ad9-c7e9dd10b438","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"jusprin-newui","slug":"glimmering-doodling-lovelace"}
