{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"473348c5-5f94-4e4d-9ad9-c7e9dd10b438","hash":"45e82aad212212909fa76bd3ffd7574d31ff49bc38e176a3ff65c64dd05467e6","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01YKBGEgEh5AdGZr8HLk5vnf","name":"SendMessage","input":{"to":"local_cea7b182-1404-4ee3-afa3-e87cbafe7c2d","summary":"First-launch confusion fixes brief","message":"Kenneth agreed to fix 23 confusing spots in the first launch; here is the full brief, please do all of it after your current step.\n\nKenneth's words: \"tell the coding agent to fix all the issues you identified, based on your recommendations\". The same brief is saved at /Users/kenneth/Library/Application Support/Claude/side-session-notes/local_4d17825a-ac19-4732-a080-7e0c1dca6d1c/first-run-confusion-fixes-2026-11-05.md. The review with screenshots, each problem pinned where it appears: https://claude.ai/artifact/91wmdS3QU8UkzbPi1zog15 (read it with the Artifact tool's read action).\n\nEvery item below is agreed. The quoted new wording is the agreed direction; small wording changes to fit the layout are fine, but keep the meaning. Where an item says \"check\", find the real value before writing it; do not invent numbers. Follow the design-system rules for any new UI (tokens only), and keep AgentUI/src/wording.test.ts passing. Most of this is in HomeUI/src/components/Onboarding.tsx, AgentGroup.tsx, PrinterCard.tsx, PrinterPickerHost.tsx, AgentUI/src/components/BalancePanel.tsx and Home/OrcaHomeBackend.cpp / OrcaImporter.cpp.\n\nWELCOME SCREEN\n1. Sign-up, not only sign-in. Today the only buttons are \"Continue with Google\" and \"Continue with email\", with \"New or existing account, same door.\" under them. Lead with signing up: the email button reads \"Sign up free\", with a small \"Already have an account? Sign in\" link. Both still send the same email code; only the words change. Remove \"New or existing account, same door.\" Apply the same to Home's \"Set up the agent\" card (it uses the same SignInDoor).\n2. Replace \"Pick how the agent should think. Change it any time in Preferences › Agent.\" with what the choice is: \"Sign up to use the AI agent, or skip it and just slice.\"\n3. Replace \"An Expert message is 5 credits.\" with what 500 credits buys in things the person does, for example \"500 credits is about 100 questions to the agent\". Check the number against the real per-message credit costs before writing it.\n4. Fold \"Your own API key — Free\" and \"Claude Code or Claude Desktop — Free · MCP server\" into one quieter link, \"Use your own AI account instead\". The screen it opens explains both options. Drop \"Free\" (an API key is paid to the AI company) and \"MCP server\" from the welcome.\n\nSIGNING IN\n5. After the email is typed, the card asks \"How do you want to sign in?\" with a Password box and \"Forgot password\". Show only \"Email me a 6-digit code\" at first, with a small \"Use a password instead\" link that reveals the password box for people who set one. Drop \"New here? The code makes your account.\" once the button itself says sign-up (item 1).\n6. Code screen: replace \"The sixth digit signs you in. Read the email on any device.\" with \"Type the code from the email. You can open it on your phone.\"\n7. Code screen: \"Use the browser instead\" becomes \"Sign in with Google instead\".\n8. Google waiting card: \"Finish signing in in your browser.\" becomes \"Finish in your browser.\"\n\nAFTER SIGNING IN\n9. \"Signed in as new@example.com · 500 credits\" (welcome card for 1.5 s, and carried to the top of the printer step and the OrcaSlicer import screen) becomes \"You got 500 free credits for signing up.\" with the email on a smaller line under it. Use the account's real credit total. Include the expiry (item 10).\n10. One name for the sign-up credits everywhere. Today: \"Your first month: 500 credits\" (welcome), \"500 credits\" (after sign-in), \"First-month credits … Expires 4 Dec\" (Home, from lotName for kind 'signup' in BalancePanel.tsx, which the Agent panel shares). Use \"free credits\" in sentences and \"Sign-up credits\" as the row name, and say when they end in the sign-in line: \"You got 500 free credits, good until 4 December.\" The welcome offer becomes \"Sign up and get 500 free credits\", with the one-month limit stated.\n11. Home's account card \"JusPrin account · Connected\" becomes \"Signed in as new@example.com\". \"Connected\" stays printer language.\n\nORCASLICER IMPORT SCREEN\n12. A tick box per printer, all ticked to start. Only ticked printers are imported. Today all eight come over together.\n13. Say which printer JusPrin will use after the import: \"JusPrin starts with Bambu Lab P1S, the printer OrcaSlicer had selected.\" If that printer is unticked, name the one that will actually be selected.\n14. \"Start fresh\" becomes \"Choose my printer instead\".\n15. The folder line: \"· 3 filaments\" breaks onto two lines at the far right. Put \"Also brings 3 filaments\" on its own line, and the folder path in smaller text.\n\nPRINTER STEP\n16. After a model is chosen, Continue stays grey with nothing on screen while the app reads that printer's settings (84 s in my run on a heavily loaded Mac; printerForm.loading). Show \"Reading this printer's settings…\" with a spinner under the nozzle buttons while it loads.\n17. Remove \"OrcaSlicer printers in another folder? Choose the folder…\" from the printer step. It shows to everyone without an OrcaSlicer folder, including people who never used OrcaSlicer. File › Import › \"Import from OrcaSlicer…\" covers this.\n18. \"Skip, and JusPrin slices for a generic 0.4 mm printer until you add yours.\" is misleading: Skip installs OrcaSlicer's \"Generic Klipper Printer\" (Custom/machine/MyKlipper 0.4 nozzle: 250 × 250 mm bed, Klipper G-code), per OrcaHomeBackend::assume_default_printer. Say what the stand-in is: \"Until you add yours, files are sliced for a 250 mm Klipper printer and may not print on other printers.\" Same fix for Home's \"No printer yet\" card and the drop-zone line that repeat it.\n\nHOME\n19. A printer added a moment ago says \"Not connected. No network connection is set up.\" For a printer that has never had a connection set up, show \"Connect it to send prints straight from JusPrin\" beside the Connect button, with no status word. Keep the existing statuses for printers that have a connection.\n20. Home's \"Set up the agent\" card never says why. Add one line at the top: \"Get 500 free credits and ask the agent to fix failed prints.\"\n\nIMPORT RESULT SCREEN\n21. With 6 of 7 items imported, the title says \"Some settings need attention\". Use \"Imported from OrcaSlicer\" as the title and show the failure in its own row.\n22. \"Not imported · its base profile, Kingroon PLA Silk, isn't in JusPrin\" becomes \"This filament is built on Kingroon PLA Silk, which JusPrin doesn't have.\" Show \"Retry failed items\" only when a failure is one a retry can fix (a file that couldn't be read), not for a missing base.\n23. Remove \"OrcaSlicer's own files were not changed.\" The screen before already says OrcaSlicer keeps its own copy.\n\nNOT IN SCOPE\nThe freeze after Import is being fixed by another session. For whoever fixes it: pressing Continue on the printer step froze the main thread for about 108 s too, inside SetupCommands::install_and_select_printer → Tab::select_preset → Plater::on_config_change → GLCanvas3D::reload_scene. Probably the same cause; unverified.\n\nDONE MEANS\nEach item checked on the real page, with a screenshot of each changed screen; the HomeUI and AgentUI tests and wording.test.ts pass; the C++ change for item 12 (ticked printers only) and item 22 (when Retry shows) has a test."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
