{"parentUuid":"dccf88a2-cd90-4e7e-a8bd-d59b538e46f8","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgmAwmv3aoLZn1xpFMZSX","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I sent all 23 fixes to the coding session, [Build the first-run flow on top of the credits branch](#local_cea7b182-1404-4ee3-afa3-e87cbafe7c2d), and it has started on them. Nothing is built or checked yet.\n\nThe brief is written as changes you've agreed to. For each spot it gives the words on screen today, the new wording or behaviour, and the files involved. It points to the review page for the screenshots. \"Done\" means each changed screen is checked on the real page with a screenshot, the interface tests pass (including the wording check), and the two code-logic changes have tests. Those two are importing only the ticked OrcaSlicer printers, and showing \"Retry\" only for failures a retry can fix.\n\nThere are three places where I told it to check before writing:\n- **What 500 credits buys.** It has to work out from real per-message costs how many questions 500 credits cover. My example of \"about 100\" is not checked.\n- **Which printer is used after the import.** If the person unticks the printer OrcaSlicer had selected, the screen must name the printer that will really be used.\n- **What \"Skip\" installs.** The new text says files are sliced for a 250 mm Klipper printer. That matches what the code installs today, so the text has to change if that printer changes.\n\nI also passed along that pressing Continue on the printer step froze the app for about 108 seconds. I marked it out of scope and flagged it for whoever is fixing the import freeze.\n\nA copy of the brief is in the shared notes folder: `/Users/kenneth/Library/Application Support/Claude/side-session-notes/local_4d17825a-ac19-4732-a080-7e0c1dca6d1c/first-run-confusion-fixes-2026-11-05.md`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":244,"cache_read_input_tokens":279787,"output_tokens":568,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":244,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":568,"cache_read_input_tokens":279787,"cache_creation_input_tokens":244,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":244},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgmAwmfAjpSdWoG1i9VsD","requestRef":"206efbba-68c5-4245-be40-312e630d9f74","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","attributionMcpServer":"ccd_turn","attributionMcpTool":"wrap_up","type":"assistant","uuid":"de1e455b-e7fb-4c8d-90ed-3377e8a1d831","timestamp":"2026-11-06T06:06:32.075Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/Library/Application Support/Claude/side-session-notes/local_4d17825a-ac19-4732-a080-7e0c1dca6d1c","sessionId":"473348c5-5f94-4e4d-9ad9-c7e9dd10b438","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"jusprin-newui","slug":"glimmering-doodling-lovelace"}
