ffort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin","sessionId":"473348c5-5f94-4e4d-9ad9-c7e9dd10b438","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"jusprin-newui","slug":"glimmering-doodling-lovelace"}
{"parentUuid":"b4d110e3-8b16-47b6-8dae-e8f008de638f","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"b789ef4c-3a30-4135-a5e8-d4380dfc1651","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Pj5YvVzGUUcTysR6A7yis2","type":"tool_result","content":"---\nname: account-billing-served-by-server\ndescription: \"2026-11-05 who draws Account's billing part; Kenneth agreed \\\"server\\\" on a premise I got wrong (server already sends prices); re-asked; designs exist on canvas boards 4a-4c, 5a-5b, 7a-7b\"\nmetadata:\n  node_type: memory\n  type: project\n  originSessionId: 7566e938-1b8f-4cc5-8b09-6c28956c5fc2\n  modified: 2026-11-06T06:10:59.343Z\n---\n\nOn 2026-11-05 I told Kenneth that if the app draws Account's plan price, a price change needs an app release. He agreed the server should draw it. That premise was wrong: `/ent/jusprin/v2/account` (tsd-enterprise `ledger/account.py`) already sends `prices` (plans with cents, the pack, credit cents) and `plan.obico_discount`, so an app-drawn price follows the server's settings with no release. I corrected it the same day and re-asked; check the conversation or ask before treating either answer as settled.\n\nWhat is designed (canvas https://claude.ai/artifact/ENCtdaz7gjynfbcy4JYbWJ): 5a/5b pricing page in the browser (Pay as you go $10/500, Hobby $10/750, Workshop $20/1000 + Standard free; $8/$16 for Obico Premium); 4a-4c Preferences › Account drawn as one app section, including \"Workshop · $16 a month\", Renews, discount line, Manage plan, purchase and reward rows, Alerts checkbox; 7a/7b savings alert above the composer; board 9 \"+500 credits\" line after buying.\n\nWhat exists: `/ent/jusprin/pricing/` is still the v1 page (Free + Unlimited $6.99/$59.99, Chargebee checkout only for `jusprin-unlimited-*`); the app's \"Get more credits\" opens it.\n\n**Why:** Kenneth's 11-02 reason for server pages: prices change often, no app release for a price change, old copies must not show old prices.\nRelated: [[one-action-to-get-more-credits]], [[v1-subscribers-grandfathered]], [[credits-boards-live-on-flow-pages]].\n---\nname: credits-boards-live-on-flow-pages\ndescription: \"Kenneth, 2026-11-02: credits boards sit on the canvas pages of their flows, not one dedicated page; only the pricing page, states overview and rules stay on Credits & plans.\"\nmetadata:\n  type: project\n---\n\nDecided after Kenneth's review, relayed by the pricing session: canvas version 69. 1a to 1d, 6a, 6b on \"On boarding experience\"; 2a to 2c, 3a to 3d, 7a to 7c on \"Compositions\" beside the Composer; 4a to 4c on \"Agent setup & Preferences\"; 8a to 8d on \"Print history\"; 0 (five rules), 5a, 5b, 9 on \"Credits & plans\".\n\n**How to apply:** new credits boards go on their flow's page through the `LAYOUT` table in `figma-mirror/tools/composer/build_credits_page.py`, with \"Credits\" in the canvas name so a search finds the set. Related: [[print-report-lives-on-history-entry]].\n---\nname: one-action-to-get-more-credits\ndescription: \"Kenneth, 2026-11-02, on the out-of-credits card: one action, \\\"Get more credits\\\", to a page that explains the options; no choosing between Buy and Subscribe with little information.\"\nmetadata:\n  node_type: memory\n  type: feedback\n  originSessionId: 3eabf4a3-87b6-4471-a4e5-b6fb9c14763a\n  modified: 2026-11-02T05:35:53.045Z\n---\n\nOn board 3c, which offered \"Buy 500 credits ($10)\" and \"Subscribe\", Kenneth asked why not simplify to \"get more credits\" and send the person to a page that clearly states the differences, \"instead of letting the user choose an option here with extremely limited amount of information and only guessing.\"\n\n**Why:** at the moment someone runs out, they can't judge a pack against a plan from a button label.\n\n**How to apply:** outside the pricing page, the action is \"Get more credits\" and it opens that page. \"New Basic chat\" isn't a purchase, but Kenneth, same day: \"if a user has <5 credits, no point for new basic chat here\", so it appears only with 5 or more credits that Basic can spend, which means free Basic messages (board 3d). The savings alert keeps \"Subscribe\" because it names one plan and shows the sums. Related: [[chat-keeps-its-model]], [[sign-up-reason-must-be-prominent]].","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"b4440cbb-3971-4415-9fc6-971ae819d1c4","timestamp":"2026-11-06T13:26:37.048Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"---\nname: account-billing-served-by-server\ndescription: \"2026-11-05 who draws Account's billing part; Kenneth agreed \\\"server\\\" on a premise I got wrong (server already sends prices); re-asked; designs exist on canvas boards 4a-4c, 5a-5b, 7a-7b\"\nmetadata:\n  node_type: memory\n  type: project\n  originSessionId: 7566e938-1b8f-4cc5-8b09-6c28956c5fc2\n  modified: 2026-11-06T06:10:59.343Z\n---\n\nOn 2026-11-05 I told Kenneth that if the app draws Account's plan price, a price change needs an app release. He agreed the server should draw it. That premise was wrong: `/ent/jusprin/v2/account` (tsd-enterprise `ledger/account.py`) already sends `prices` (plans with cents, the pack, credit cents) and `plan.obico_discount`, so an app-drawn price follows the server's settings with no release. I corrected it the same day and re-asked; check the conversation or ask before treating either answer as settled.\n\nWhat is designed (canvas https://claude.ai/artifact/ENCtdaz7gjynfbcy4JYbWJ): 5a/5b pricing page in the browser (Pay as you go $10/500, Hobby $10/750, Workshop $20/1000 + Standard free; $8/$16 for Obico Premium); 4a-4c Preferences › Account drawn as one app section, including \"Workshop · $16 a month\", Renews, discount line, Manage plan, purchase and reward rows, Alerts checkbox; 7a/7b savings alert above the composer; board 9 \"+500 credits\" line after buying.\n\nWhat exists: `/ent/jusprin/pricing/` is still the v1 page (Free + Unlimited $6.99/$59.99, Chargebee checkout only for `jusprin-unlimited-*`); the app's \"Get more credits\" opens it.\n\n**Why:** Kenneth's 11-02 reason for server pages: prices change often, no app release for a price change, old copies must not show old prices.\nRelated: [[one-action-to-get-more-credits]], [[v1-subscribers-grandfathered]], [[credits-boards-live-on-flow-pages]].\n---\nname: credits-boards-live-on-flow-pages\ndescription: \"Kenneth, 2026-11-02: credits boards sit on the canvas pages of their flows, not one dedicated page; only the pricing page, states overview and rules stay on Credits & plans.\"\nmetadata:\n  type: project\n---\n\nDecided after Kenneth's review, relayed by the pricing session: canvas version 69. 1a to 1d, 6a, 6b on \"On boarding experience\"; 2a to 2c, 3a to 3d, 7a to 7c on \"Compositions\" beside the Composer; 4a to 4c on \"Agent setup & Preferences\"; 8a to 8d on \"Print history\"; 0 (five rules), 5a, 5b, 9 on \"Credits & plans\".\n\n**How to apply:** new credits boards go on their flow's page through the `LAYOUT` table in `figma-mirror/tools/composer/build_credits_page.py`, with \"Credits\" in the canvas name so a search finds the set. Related: [[print-report-lives-on-history-entry]].\n---\nname: one-action-to-get-more-credits\ndescription: \"Kenneth, 2026-11-02, on the out-of-credits card: one action, \\\"Get more credits\\\", to a page that explains the options; no choosing between Buy and Subscribe with little information.\"\nmetadata:\n  node_type: memory\n  type: feedback\n  originSessionId: 3eabf4a3-87b6-4471-a4e5-b6fb9c14763a\n  modified: 2026-11-02T05:35:53.045Z\n---\n\nOn board 3c, which offered \"Buy 500 credits ($10)\" and \"Subscribe\", Kenneth asked why not simplify to \"get more credits\" and send the person to a page that clearly states the differences, \"instead of letting the user choose an option here with extremely limited amount of information and only guessing.\"\n\n**Why:** at the moment someone runs out, they can't judge a pack against a plan from a button label.\n\n**How to apply:** outside the pricing page, the action is \"Get more credits\" and it opens that page. \"New Basic chat\" isn't a purchase, but Kenneth, same day: \"if a user has <5 credits, no point for new basic chat here\", so it appears only with 5 or more credits that Basic can spend, which means free Basic messages (board 3d). The savings alert keeps \"Subscribe\" because it names one plan and shows the sums. Related: [[chat-keeps-its-model]], [[sign-up-reason-must-be-prominent]].","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"b4d110e3-8b16-47b6-8dae-e8f008de638f","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/.claude/projects/-Users-kenneth-Projects-JusPrin/memory","sessionId":"473348c5-5f94-4e4d-9ad9-c7e9dd10b438","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"jusprin-newui","slug":"glimmering-doodling-lovelace"}
