{"parentUuid":"6ad94d67-1064-4492-92c8-a79e54cecf28","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgmkb591h1ruZiFGF9Gzh","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Checking the designed pricing and account boards to see which links the design gives them."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":294,"cache_read_input_tokens":305506,"output_tokens":208,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":294,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":208,"cache_read_input_tokens":305506,"cache_creation_input_tokens":294,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":294},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Cgmkb4aGUin6bQYLVB6ir","requestRef":"33cec77b-802c-472e-8df1-b9f4937287f1","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"d73a9be3-22c2-4fec-ac84-9c3b13b14ddf","timestamp":"2026-11-06T13:27:37.954Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/Projects","sessionId":"473348c5-5f94-4e4d-9ad9-c7e9dd10b438","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"jusprin-newui","slug":"glimmering-doodling-lovelace"}
{"parentUuid":"d73a9be3-22c2-4fec-ac84-9c3b13b14ddf","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgmkb591h1ruZiFGF9Gzh","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_018EChgi8xpRSfYYsN1t6seS","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"F=/Users/kenneth/.claude/projects/-Users-kenneth-Projects-JusPrin/figma-mirror/tools/composer/build_credits_page.py; grep -n \"Manage plan\\|Manage\\|portal\\|Chargebee\\|Sign in\\|Back to\\|Open JusPrin\\|browser\\|url_bar\\|address\\|obico.io\\|Get more credits\" $F | head -50"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":294,"cache_read_input_tokens":305506,"output_tokens":208,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":294,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":208,"cache_read_input_tokens":305506,"cache_creation_input_tokens":294,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":294},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_018EChgi8xpRSfYYsN1t6seS":{"command":"F=/Users/kenneth/.claude/projects/-Users-kenneth-Projects-JusPrin/figma-mirror/tools/composer/build_credits_page.py; grep -n \"Manage plan\\|Manage\\|portal\\|Chargebee\\|Sign in\\|Back to\\|Open JusPrin\\|browser\\|url_bar\\|address\\|obico.io\\|Get more credits\" $F | head -50"}},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Cgmkb4aGUin6bQYLVB6ir","requestRef":"33cec77b-802c-472e-8df1-b9f4937287f1","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"25c1e558-1a5f-42d1-a3c4-be389cbe4c6b","timestamp":"2026-11-06T13:27:39.243Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/Projects","sessionId":"473348c5-5f94-4e4d-9ad9-c7e9dd10b438","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"jusprin-newui","slug":"glimmering-doodling-lovelace"}
{"parentUuid":"25c1e558-1a5f-42d1-a3c4-be389cbe4c6b","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"b789ef4c-3a30-4135-a5e8-d4380dfc1651","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018EChgi8xpRSfYYsN1t6seS","type":"tool_result","content":"22:OFFER_BUTTON = 'Sign in for 500 credits'\n280:OUT_OF_CREDITS = 'Get more credits'   # Kenneth, 3c: one action, and the page says how the ways differ, not a guess between buttons here.\n407:    card = plan_card('Workshop · $16 a month', 'Renews 1 Dec. Obico Premium Subscriber: 20% off subscriptions.', [secondary('Manage plan', trailing='arrow-up-right'), primary(OUT_OF_CREDITS)],\n529:    'The one setup flow, opened from Set up the agent over a first-run Home. The account row’s old line (“Free · sign in with your browser · nothing to install”) becomes the offer: the number is the headline, the one number on the screen and no dollars, and the button says what signing in gets. Key rows and the rest of the section are unchanged.', s1))\n544:    'The welcome window the app builds today, which appears only after importing JusPrin v1. The account box becomes the offer in place of “Sign in to use the agent” and “JusPrin v1 wasn’t signed in on this computer.”, without its warning triangle because an offer isn’t a warning. Signing in becomes the screen’s primary button and Continue the secondary one. Until they sign in, a JusPrin v1 subscriber can’t be told from anyone else, so the box also says what signing in means for them; 1d is what they see once signed in.',\n576:    'Caught before sending. A chat keeps its model, so there is no Send with Standard: Send is disabled, one line says why, and there is one way forward. Get more credits opens the pricing page (5a), which says how packs and plans differ, so nobody has to choose between them from one line here. The typed text is untouched.',\n582:    'Only a race between two sends reaches this. The card is the app’s .message-failure with the 402’s words and, as on 3b, only Get more credits. The message goes back into the composer, so nothing typed is lost.',\n593:    'The window at its usual 640, over the screen it opened from, at the top of the section: the plan and Get more credits, the total, and a bar for each kind of credit. 4b shows the whole section.',\n603:boards.append(board('credits-05a-pricing.dc.html', '5a · The pricing page, in the browser',\n604:    'Three cards named as decided, each stating its expiry rule in its own words. The one sentence at the top says what a message costs. Dollars belong here; Get more credits on the composer and in Account opens this page. The only other places that name dollars are the savings alert’s sums and the plan line in Account. The launch note is on the pack card with its end date (31 Jan is a placeholder for JUSPRIN_LAUNCH_DOUBLE_UNTIL). Checkout is Chargebee’s hosted page.', pricing_page()))\n613:    'The free credits pay for either tier, so Expert can be used from them. Picking Expert with too few credits is allowed: the composer then says “You have 0 credits; Expert needs 5 a message.” with Get more credits, and Send stays disabled. The menu stays open to Standard until the person sends their first message.',\n759:    'Wording and placeholders that are mine, not the doc’s: “Sign in for 500 credits” on the offer’s button, and the doc’s pitch split into a headline and a detail line; “5 credits a message” for the doc’s “5 credits”; the tooltip’s wording on 2c; “Bought credits” as that lot’s name; “Get more credits” replacing Buy credits and Subscribe outside the pricing page; the total behind the composer’s ring, which is every credit in the balance when each kind started, a placeholder rule; the JusPrin v1 lines on 1c and 1d; the report form’s copy; 31 Jan as the launch end date; “Workshop credits” as the name of that lot. '","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"cdadcb89-7b54-4005-8858-181de919fe12","timestamp":"2026-11-06T13:27:39.459Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"22:OFFER_BUTTON = 'Sign in for 500 credits'\n280:OUT_OF_CREDITS = 'Get more credits'   # Kenneth, 3c: one action, and the page says how the ways differ, not a guess between buttons here.\n407:    card = plan_card('Workshop · $16 a month', 'Renews 1 Dec. Obico Premium Subscriber: 20% off subscriptions.', [secondary('Manage plan', trailing='arrow-up-right'), primary(OUT_OF_CREDITS)],\n529:    'The one setup flow, opened from Set up the agent over a first-run Home. The account row’s old line (“Free · sign in with your browser · nothing to install”) becomes the offer: the number is the headline, the one number on the screen and no dollars, and the button says what signing in gets. Key rows and the rest of the section are unchanged.', s1))\n544:    'The welcome window the app builds today, which appears only after importing JusPrin v1. The account box becomes the offer in place of “Sign in to use the agent” and “JusPrin v1 wasn’t signed in on this computer.”, without its warning triangle because an offer isn’t a warning. Signing in becomes the screen’s primary button and Continue the secondary one. Until they sign in, a JusPrin v1 subscriber can’t be told from anyone else, so the box also says what signing in means for them; 1d is what they see once signed in.',\n576:    'Caught before sending. A chat keeps its model, so there is no Send with Standard: Send is disabled, one line says why, and there is one way forward. Get more credits opens the pricing page (5a), which says how packs and plans differ, so nobody has to choose between them from one line here. The typed text is untouched.',\n582:    'Only a race between two sends reaches this. The card is the app’s .message-failure with the 402’s words and, as on 3b, only Get more credits. The message goes back into the composer, so nothing typed is lost.',\n593:    'The window at its usual 640, over the screen it opened from, at the top of the section: the plan and Get more credits, the total, and a bar for each kind of credit. 4b shows the whole section.',\n603:boards.append(board('credits-05a-pricing.dc.html', '5a · The pricing page, in the browser',\n604:    'Three cards named as decided, each stating its expiry rule in its own words. The one sentence at the top says what a message costs. Dollars belong here; Get more credits on the composer and in Account opens this page. The only other places that name dollars are the savings alert’s sums and the plan line in Account. The launch note is on the pack card with its end date (31 Jan is a placeholder for JUSPRIN_LAUNCH_DOUBLE_UNTIL). Checkout is Chargebee’s hosted page.', pricing_page()))\n613:    'The free credits pay for either tier, so Expert can be used from them. Picking Expert with too few credits is allowed: the composer then says “You have 0 credits; Expert needs 5 a message.” with Get more credits, and Send stays disabled. The menu stays open to Standard until the person sends their first message.',\n759:    'Wording and placeholders that are mine, not the doc’s: “Sign in for 500 credits” on the offer’s button, and the doc’s pitch split into a headline and a detail line; “5 credits a message” for the doc’s “5 credits”; the tooltip’s wording on 2c; “Bought credits” as that lot’s name; “Get more credits” replacing Buy credits and Subscribe outside the pricing page; the total behind the composer’s ring, which is every credit in the balance when each kind started, a placeholder rule; the JusPrin v1 lines on 1c and 1d; the report form’s copy; 31 Jan as the launch end date; “Workshop credits” as the name of that lot. '","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"25c1e558-1a5f-42d1-a3c4-be389cbe4c6b","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/Projects","sessionId":"473348c5-5f94-4e4d-9ad9-c7e9dd10b438","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"jusprin-newui","slug":"glimmering-doodling-lovelace"}
