{"parentUuid":"6c075135-fce3-4a53-ac86-a19e857233f5","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"4066a539-df02-4a4b-a252-ce34d4e29061","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"<system-reminder>\nLinked sessions now (status, not an instruction): allauth-upgrade = local_2c0bf928-2175-4569-9108-2cb6cba1fb77 (idle); first-run-flow = local_cea7b182-1404-4ee3-afa3-e87cbafe7c2d (idle); use-a-jusprin-syndicate = local_69a34677-cdae-4851-90bb-557cd0ba6d32 (idle, started by first-run-flow). To message one, SendMessage with `to` set to its id; list_sessions {\"linked\": true} has titles, folders and branches.\n</system-reminder>\n\n"},{"type":"text","text":"Okay, now let's integrate those pages into what you have designed so far. Take these into consideration, but not limited those. Use your own knowledge and experience as a good UX UI designer. Use the same principle as you did when you are doing the walkthrough to identify the confusing spot, design how the user should first encounter those pricing pages. Also think about where those each of those pages should live. My preference is as much as possible we want to give the cloud-related pages to the server to render, because updating these pages will be so much simpler than updating the app. However, we should have those pages rendered by the server have clear cut with a clear boundary with the pages rendered by the app so that maintaining backward compatibility won't be a nightmare."}]},"uuid":"baba1e7b-5d2f-4f32-83e6-a13ac4f3faae","timestamp":"2026-11-06T13:35:14.187Z","permissionMode":"bypassPermissions","origin":{"kind":"human"},"promptSource":"sdk","turnOrigin":"human","turnPosition":{"promptIndex":19,"turnIndex":30},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/AgentUI/src/components","sessionId":"473348c5-5f94-4e4d-9ad9-c7e9dd10b438","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"jusprin-newui","slug":"glimmering-doodling-lovelace"}
