{"parentUuid":"04bc9a16-5856-471c-98eb-f3e1f1244cc5","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"4066a539-df02-4a4b-a252-ce34d4e29061","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016xZe7T6sgjrjUAK3sdLJd8","type":"tool_result","content":"RULES = [('One word, one unit, credits only.', 'It is “credits”, never coins or tokens. A balance is a number of credits and nothing else. Prices in messages appear only on the picker options, the stop card, the pricing page sentence and one scale line under the first-month offer. Dollars appear only where money changes hands.'),\n         ('Credits move only when the person sends a message.', 'Turns the app starts are free, so the balance never changes without a message from the person. On Workshop, Standard messages cost 0 credits.'),\n         ('Credits are named by kind, with a date.', 'Every credit pays for either tier, so bars are grouped only by when credits expire: First-month credits, Free credits and Bought credits, one bar each, and a plan’s monthly credits the same way. After the first month, accounts without a plan get 50 free credits a month, pack holders too; the first month has only the 500. An expiring lot expires one month from the day it was granted; a plan’s credits expire with its billing cycle. The breakdown says once that expiring credits are used first.'),\n         ('Say the number before the boundary, not at it.', 'When the balance runs low the composer says so once, “About 25 credits left”, so reaching it is never news.'),\n         ('Nothing typed is lost.', 'A message that can’t be sent stays in the composer, and nothing stops silently.')]\nboards.append(board('credits-00-rules.dc.html', '0 · Five rules wherever a person meets credits',\n    'The boards themselves sit with their flows: On boarding experience, Compositions (beside the Composer), Agent setup & Preferences and Print history. Search “credits” to find them all.',\n/Users/kenneth/.claude/projects/-Users-kenneth-Projects-JusPrin/figma-mirror/work-credits:\ncredits-boards.json\nproject\nruntime\n\n/Users/kenneth/.claude/projects/-Users-kenneth-Projects-JusPrin/figma-mirror/work-first-run-v2:\nlive\nlive2\nlive3\nproject\nrender\nrender-dark\nruntime\n25 credits left and ring for free credits 2026-11-02, from Kenneth directly: 3a, 6a, 6b, canvas.json, before 1793640736-672c, after 1793641329-8c74 (version 77), label \"25 credits left; ring for free credits\".\n\nExpiry by grant date, no reverse alert, no thinking picker on Standard 2026-11-02, Kenneth's review relayed by the pricing session: 0, 2a, 2b, 3a, 3e, 4a, 4b, 4c, 6a, 6b, 9, canvas.json, 7c removed, before 1793641329-8c74, after 1793641941-ae85 (version 78), label \"Credits: expiry by grant date, no \n\nNo free credits in the first month 2026-11-02, Kenneth relayed by the pricing session: 0, 2a, 2b, 2c, 3e, 4a, 4b, 5a, 5b, 9, canvas.json, before 1793641941-ae85, after 1793642611-3f5d (version 79), label \"Credits: no free credits in the first month\".\nPrint-report clawback removed 2026-11-02, Kenneth in the build session: 3a, 4c, canvas.json, after 1793650696-c09d (version 81), label \"Credits: print-report clawback removed\".\nNo daily limit on print reports 2026-11-02, Kenneth in the build session: 8b, after 1793651048-7275 (version 82), label \"Credits: no daily limit on print reports\".\nFirst-run flow 2026-11-02, asked for by the session designing the replacement for the onboarding wizard: 13 new boards first-run-01a to first-run-07 and canvas.json (two new notes), before 1793658772-45ce, after 1793662061-b48d (version 84), label \"First-run flow boards\". Builder `tools/composer/bui\nFirst-run variants A and B 2026-11-02, asked for by the session designing the replacement for the onboarding wizard: the 13 first-run-NN boards renamed and redrawn as first-run-a-01a to first-run-a-07 (the assumed-printer rule), 11 new first-run-b-01 to first-run-b-06, canvas.json (four notes), befo\nFirst launch: one welcome screen 2026-11-02, Kenneth via the pricing session: variants A and B withdrawn (24 first-run-a-*/first-run-b-* boards and their 4 notes removed; nothing else on the page had moved for them), 3 new boards first-run-welcome-01-clip-beat-1, -02-clip-final-frame, -03-clip-story\nWelcome screen without shell chrome 2026-11-02, Kenneth via the pricing session: first-run-welcome-01 and -02 lose the \"JusPrin › Agent\" header and the footer sentence, and gain the JusPrin lockup top-left (OrcaSlicer_horizontal_light/dark.svg uploaded as assets 2c8a9c17… and 8169ceb4…, 43 px \nFirst launch, the full flow 2026-11-02, Kenneth (\"Draw them\") via the pricing session: 8 new boards first-run-04-welcome-sign-in-waiting, -05-welcome-signed-in, -06-preferences-over-welcome, -07-orcaslicer-import, -08-add-printer, -09-home-after-sign-in, -10-home-after-just-slice, -11-flow (1600 x 9\n\nFirst-run sign-in door (2026-11-03, Kenneth: \"Yes, build it\", then \"update the board on canvas to reflect the new design\"): canvas\nhttps://claude.ai/artifact/ENCtdaz7gjynfbcy4JYbWJ before 1793743067-978a, after 1793744174-5990 (version 93), label \"First-run\nsign-in door, email steps\". Onboarding page: 01, 02 draw the built door (Continue with Google, \"or\", email field), 04 the\nbrowser-wait card, 05 the signed-in line, 06 and 10 the corrected scale line and Home's door; new row y 7100 holds 12 to 16 (email\nchoice, wrong password, code, wrong code, spent code). Rows 07-08, 09-10 and the superseded wizard moved down 940. Google mark\nuploaded as /_blob/1989511be90a76940f6415e6e4d55ab9. Builder tools/composer/build_first_run_page.py; work copy\nwork-first-run-door/ (project/ds is a symlink for rendering, not published). Board 03 not republished (renderVals drift only).\nWatch stopped after publishing.\n\nHome set-up card, 2026-11-03: canvas version 94 (1793745150-db9e), board 10 redrawn with the email field above its button (app commit follows). Watch stays stopped.\n\nFirst launch, printer step and page order 2026-1