{"parentUuid":"a98c76eb-1e70-47f0-9458-57b67c67f2f6","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"auto_mode","autoModeConsentFlow":false,"finishExposedWork":false,"bashFirst":true,"bashFirstSteer":"relaxed","steerOnly":true,"bypass":true},"type":"attachment","uuid":"a6dd278f-ff29-4ff1-8bc0-783c866c1f71","timestamp":"2026-11-06T13:40:17.342Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nWhile bypass permissions mode is active:\n\nYou can do much of your work through the Bash tool when it is the simpler route: read files with cat, head, or sed -n, search with grep and find, and make small, mechanical file changes with sed, heredocs, or short scripts instead of the dedicated Read, Edit, or Write tools. The choice is yours: prefer Edit or Write when a shell edit would be fragile, such as exact or multi-line replacements, or sed/awk flags that differ between GNU and BSD/macOS.\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/Projects","sessionId":"473348c5-5f94-4e4d-9ad9-c7e9dd10b438","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"jusprin-newui","slug":"glimmering-doodling-lovelace"}
