ee checkout, as today.\n- Thank-you page (new; replaces today's redirect to the v1 chat at /jusprin/v1.0/embedded_chat/).\n- Billing (new): plan in dollars, Change plan, Cancel plan, Chargebee portal for payment method and invoices, Delete account.\n- The savings alert's sentence and sums.\n\n## The contract between them (the only part old app versions depend on)\n\n1. GET /v2/account, as today. Fields are only added, never renamed or removed; the app ignores fields it doesn't know. The app reads it again whenever its window becomes active, which is how \"+1,000 credits\" appears after paying.\n2. New: POST /v2/web_link {page: \"prices\" | \"billing\", from: \"welcome\" | \"composer_low\" | \"out_of_credits\" | \"preferences\" | \"alert\"} → {url}. When signed in, the URL carries a one-time sign-in token (single use, about 60 s) so the browser opens as the app's account, whichever way the person signed in. Signed out, the URL has no token. The server answers these page names forever; an unknown name opens Credits and plans. Today the app builds the URL itself (AgentConfiguration.cpp cloud_pricing_url, gateway + \"/ent/jusprin/pricing/\"), so this replaces that.\n3. The account answer's unused `suggestion` slot (web_ent/jusprin/ledger/account.py) carries {text, page}. The app shows the text as written and opens the page through a page link.\n\n## Confusing spots this fixes\n\n- After signing in with email in the app, the browser is probably signed out (unverified), so a person could buy on a different account. Fixed by the page link.\n- \"Pay as you go\" shown as the plan of someone who never paid. Now \"No plan\".\n- The pricing card said \"500 credits\" while its launch note said \"$10 buys 1,000\". The card now says 1,000 with \"double the usual 500\" under it.\n- The pricing page showed neither balance nor current plan. Now a line at the top says both, and the current plan's button reads \"Your plan\".\n- Nothing after paying said to go back to the app. The thank-you page does.\n- The app's Account and a server account page would share a name. The server page is \"Billing\".\n- Nothing defined where Manage plan went. It becomes \"Billing ↗\".\n- An expired link lands on the signed-out pricing page with a line saying why, not an error.\n\n## Server work this needs\n\n- web_link endpoint and token sign-in (new).\n- Pricing page v2 (the v1 page at /ent/jusprin/pricing/ offers Free and Unlimited $6.99).\n- Thank-you and Billing pages.\n- Moving the savings-alert arithmetic from the app into `suggestion`.\n\n## App work this needs\n\n- Call web_link instead of building the pricing URL.\n- Refresh the account answer on window activation.\n- Preferences › Account: \"No plan\", drop \"$16 a month\" and the discount line, \"Billing ↗\".\n- Show `suggestion` when present.\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"e92beab4-749c-4ed3-9f4d-12db27dfec92","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/.claude/projects/-Users-kenneth-Projects-JusPrin/figma-mirror","sessionId":"473348c5-5f94-4e4d-9ad9-c7e9dd10b438","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"jusprin-newui","slug":"glimmering-doodling-lovelace"}
