{"parentUuid":"5d93316f-c12f-4ee9-a5fa-2775a717c5b0","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgmmyQvc8E9yCgnv9GF65","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've added ten new boards to the \"Credits & plans\" page of the canvas (https://claude.ai/artifact/ENCtdaz7gjynfbcy4JYbWJ, version 118). They show which money pages the app draws and which the server draws, and how a person first reaches the pricing page. They sit below the existing pricing boards. The spec is at [money-pages-app-server-split-2026-11-06.md](money-pages-app-server-split-2026-11-06.md). Everything here is a proposal: nothing is approved and no code has changed.\n\n**The split.** The app shows credits and the server sells them.\n- **The app** draws the credit counts, the low and out-of-credits warnings, usage per chat, and a \"+1,000 credits\" line after buying.\n- **The server** draws every page with a dollar amount or a payment form:\n  - the pricing page;\n  - Chargebee's checkout;\n  - a new thank-you page;\n  - a new Billing page, where you change or cancel a plan, reach payment method and invoices, and delete the account.\n\n**What old app versions depend on.** Only three things cross between the app and the server:\n1. **The account answer the app already reads.** The server may only add fields to it, never rename or remove them. The app reads it again whenever its window becomes active, which is how new credits appear after paying.\n2. **A new page-link request.** The app asks for \"prices\" or \"billing\" and gets back a URL that signs the browser in as the same account, once, for about a minute. The server must answer those two names forever. A name it doesn't know opens the pricing page.\n3. **An unused field in the account answer for server-written alerts.** The savings alert's text and sums would come from there, so new offers need no app release.\n\n**How a person first meets prices:**\n1. The welcome card says \"Sign up and get 500 free credits\", how long they last, and what comes after. A \"See prices ↗\" link opens the pricing page signed out, with \"Sign in to buy\" buttons.\n2. Later, \"Get more credits\" opens the same page already signed in. A line at the top says the person's balance and which account the purchase goes to.\n3. After checkout, the thank-you page says what was added and tells them to go back to the app.\n4. Back in the app, the typed message is still in the box and Send is enabled.\n\n**Confusing spots the design fixes:**\n- **Wrong account.** After signing in with email in the app, the browser may open signed out (I haven't tested this). The person could then buy on a different account.\n- **\"Pay as you go\" as a plan name.** Someone who never paid sees it as their plan. They now see \"No plan\".\n- **500 or 1,000?** The launch-offer card said \"500 credits\" while its note said \"$10 buys 1,000\". The card now says 1,000.\n- **Dead ends.** The pricing page didn't show the current plan, and nothing after paying said to return to the app.\n- **Leftover v1 links.** The page after checkout today sends the person to the v1 chat, and nothing said where \"Manage plan\" goes. The first is replaced by the thank-you page, and \"Manage plan\" becomes \"Billing ↗\".\n\n**Decision needed: should all dollar amounts move out of the app?** It's your call because it changes boards you've already seen. Two places in the app would lose their dollars:\n- **The Workshop plan line** in Preferences › Account would lose \"$16 a month\" and the Obico discount line. They would appear on the Billing page instead.\n- **The savings alert's dollar sums** would be written by the server instead of computed by the app.\n\nIf you approve, price changes never need an app release, but a person has to open the browser to see what they pay. If you don't, the account answer must carry prices and the app keeps formatting them. I recommend approving. Should all dollar amounts move out of the app?\n\n**Decision needed: should the server build the one-time sign-in link?** This is new server work: one endpoint plus a short-lived, single-use sign-in token. Without it, the browser may be signed in as nobody, or as another account, when someone buys. The cheaper option is to always open the pricing page signed out and make people sign in again, which costs a step at the moment they want to pay. I recommend building the link. Should the server build it?\n\nSeparately: the fix list I sent the first-run coding session removes the \"OrcaSlicer printers in another folder?\" line from the printer step. You approved keeping that line on 2026-11-03, and your later \"fix all the issues\" reverses it. Say if you want it kept."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":447,"cache_read_input_tokens":212126,"output_tokens":1442,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":447,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1442,"cache_read_input_tokens":212126,"cache_creation_input_tokens":447,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":447},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgmmyQfETSt2CCFKmLXUH","requestRef":"046ecb2e-d6f1-4d56-a464-b152a2a74734","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","attributionMcpServer":"ccd_turn","attributionMcpTool":"wrap_up","type":"assistant","uuid":"4c83420d-ccde-4810-8cd4-6254ed0809a8","timestamp":"2026-11-06T13:46:01.819Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/.claude/projects/-Users-kenneth-Projects-JusPrin/figma-mirror","sessionId":"473348c5-5f94-4e4d-9ad9-c7e9dd10b438","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"jusprin-newui","slug":"glimmering-doodling-lovelace"}
