{"parentUuid":"f1cbf0e4-8fd9-4af7-803c-596cd8032501","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgmr8aptwu8kat61zf8Ad","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5325,"cache_read_input_tokens":212573,"output_tokens":1071,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":420},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5325,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1071,"cache_read_input_tokens":212573,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5325,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5325},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[{"type":"thinking_dropped","path":"messages.2.content.0","reason":"prefix_binding_mismatch"}],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":5177,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Cgmr8Xu2CrMXSZ7AdywMV","requestRef":"406091f7-5f20-4675-8787-08df07aa4f7d","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"1489cde3-83f7-48e3-a02f-1401cb06eceb","timestamp":"2026-11-06T14:40:25.379Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin","sessionId":"473348c5-5f94-4e4d-9ad9-c7e9dd10b438","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"jusprin-newui","slug":"glimmering-doodling-lovelace"}
{"parentUuid":"1489cde3-83f7-48e3-a02f-1401cb06eceb","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgmr8aptwu8kat61zf8Ad","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Here's the trade-off as I see it, plus a middle option I should have offered the first time.\n\n**What the boundary is really protecting against.** The risk isn't that a dollar sign appears in the app. The risk is that the app holds money logic: prices, discounts, the savings-alert arithmetic, how a plan is described. Once that logic ships, it's frozen in every installed version. If the Workshop price changes or the Obico discount ends, old apps keep showing the old number for months.\n\n**What my proposal costs.** Someone on Workshop opens Preferences › Account and sees \"Workshop, renews 1 Dec\", but not what they pay. To find out, they click Billing ↗ and wait for a browser page. The savings alert loses its dollars too, and that alert was supposed to persuade with a dollar figure (\"Hobby would have saved you $5.00\").\n\n**The middle option.** Instead of \"the app never shows dollars\", the rule could be \"the app never works out or formats money; it shows text the server wrote\". The account answer would carry a ready-made line such as \"$16 a month · Obico Premium: 20% off\". The app would print it as is. The savings alert works the same way through the unused field for server-written alerts. Price changes still need no release, because the app never knows what a price is. And the person still sees the price where they look for it.\n\nWhat it costs is a small rule the server must keep forever: those lines are plain text the app shows without parsing. That's the same kind of promise as the page names, so it doesn't add a new kind of risk.\n\n**What I'm unsure about.** I think Claude's and ChatGPT's apps show the plan name in their settings and send billing to the web, but I haven't checked, so treat that as a guess. I could look before you decide.\n\nI now lean toward the middle option over my original rule. If you agree, I'll put the price line back on the Account board and the dollar figure back in the alert, both marked as server-written.\n\nWhich part do you want to dig into: where dollars may appear, the one-time sign-in link, or which pages the server owns?"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5325,"cache_read_input_tokens":212573,"output_tokens":1071,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":420},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5325,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1071,"cache_read_input_tokens":212573,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5325,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5325},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[{"type":"thinking_dropped","path":"messages.2.content.0","reason":"prefix_binding_mismatch"}],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Cgmr8Xu2CrMXSZ7AdywMV","requestRef":"406091f7-5f20-4675-8787-08df07aa4f7d","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"bee35cec-74e8-4daf-ba68-23a53d7e8297","timestamp":"2026-11-06T14:40:32.798Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin","sessionId":"473348c5-5f94-4e4d-9ad9-c7e9dd10b438","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"jusprin-newui","slug":"glimmering-doodling-lovelace"}
