{"parentUuid":"f634ef3e-1879-4780-8f6c-1ab3ce14a4f7","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"7e1818b2-a86b-46e5-abf5-d2df9e7fae27","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01S832BiF5Zp58RZvKkzq1As","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Chargebee hosted checkout inside webview mobile app 3D Secure popup support\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"# React Native Wrapper\",\"url\":\"https://chargebee.com/checkout-portal-docs/react-native-wrapper-for-mobile.html\"},{\"title\":\"New in Chargebee: Explore Reveal and understand your payment performance end-to-end.Try Now\",\"url\":\"https://www.chargebee.com/docs/billing/1.0/hosted-capabilities/mobile-react-native-wrapper\"},{\"title\":\"Introducing the Chargebee CLI\",\"url\":\"https://www.chargebee.com/docs/hosted-checkout.html\"},{\"title\":\"Introducing the Chargebee CLI\",\"url\":\"https://chargebee.com/docs/2.0/checkout.html\"},{\"title\":\"New in Chargebee: Explore Reveal and understand your payment performance end-to-end.Try Now\",\"url\":\"https://www.chargebee.com/docs/1.0/hosted-checkout.html\"},{\"title\":\"New in Chargebee: Explore Reveal and understand your payment performance end-to-end.Try Now\",\"url\":\"https://www.chargebee.com/docs/2.0/hosted-checkout.html\"},{\"title\":\"New in Chargebee: Explore Reveal and understand your payment performance end-to-end.Try Now\",\"url\":\"https://www.chargebee.com/docs/billing/2.0/kb/billing/what-is-the-hosted-pagescheckout-pages-of-chargebee\"}]\n\nThe search confirms the basic setup but doesn't say how 3D Secure popups behave inside a WebView.\n\n- **WebView wrapper exists:** Chargebee's React Native Wrapper renders Chargebee-hosted checkout pages within a WebView component in your mobile app.\n- **Restricted use case:** Chargebee says use this wrapper only to sell physical goods and services in your mobile apps. Digital goods must go through in-app purchases on iOS and Android.\n- **3DS handling:** Chargebee's docs say that once the payment is authorized (including any 3D Secure or wallet authentication), the order completes and the subscription is created immediately, even if the customer does not return to the next page. This suggests 3DS is handled within the checkout flow, but it doesn't describe popup or WebView specifics.\n- **In-app layout:** Chargebee's older docs say the in-app layout displays as a modal popup. Chargebee.js loads the checkout UI in an iframe that Chargebee manages.\n- **Gap:** None of the results cover whether a 3DS challenge opens as a nested popup or redirect inside the WebView, or how that interacts with the app's WebView settings. That would need Chargebee's React Native wrapper docs or a support ticket to confirm.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"e8effc48-8b87-4152-bfe2-3ff7220322b6","timestamp":"2026-11-06T14:42:58.627Z","toolUseResult":{"query":"Chargebee hosted checkout inside webview mobile app 3D Secure popup support","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01RVySBXfWB3FEnRKvkndf4d","content":[{"title":"# React Native Wrapper","url":"https://chargebee.com/checkout-portal-docs/react-native-wrapper-for-mobile.html"},{"title":"New in Chargebee: Explore Reveal and understand your payment performance end-to-end.Try Now","url":"https://www.chargebee.com/docs/billing/1.0/hosted-capabilities/mobile-react-native-wrapper"},{"title":"Introducing the Chargebee CLI","url":"https://www.chargebee.com/docs/hosted-checkout.html"},{"title":"Introducing the Chargebee CLI","url":"https://chargebee.com/docs/2.0/checkout.html"},{"title":"New in Chargebee: Explore Reveal and understand your payment performance end-to-end.Try Now","url":"https://www.chargebee.com/docs/1.0/hosted-checkout.html"},{"title":"New in Chargebee: Explore Reveal and understand your payment performance end-to-end.Try Now","url":"https://www.chargebee.com/docs/2.0/hosted-checkout.html"},{"title":"New in Chargebee: Explore Reveal and understand your payment performance end-to-end.Try Now","url":"https://www.chargebee.com/docs/billing/2.0/kb/billing/what-is-the-hosted-pagescheckout-pages-of-chargebee"}]},"The search confirms the basic setup but doesn't say how 3D Secure popups behave inside a WebView.\n\n- **WebView wrapper exists:** Chargebee's React Native Wrapper renders Chargebee-hosted checkout pages within a WebView component in your mobile app.\n- **Restricted use case:** Chargebee says use this wrapper only to sell physical goods and services in your mobile apps. Digital goods must go through in-app purchases on iOS and Android.\n- **3DS handling:** Chargebee's docs say that once the payment is authorized (including any 3D Secure or wallet authentication), the order completes and the subscription is created immediately, even if the customer does not return to the next page. This suggests 3DS is handled within the checkout flow, but it doesn't describe popup or WebView specifics.\n- **In-app layout:** Chargebee's older docs say the in-app layout displays as a modal popup. Chargebee.js loads the checkout UI in an iframe that Chargebee manages.\n- **Gap:** None of the results cover whether a 3DS challenge opens as a nested popup or redirect inside the WebView, or how that interacts with the app's WebView settings. That would need Chargebee's React Native wrapper docs or a support ticket to confirm."],"durationSeconds":7.59101912500002,"searchCount":1},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"f634ef3e-1879-4780-8f6c-1ab3ce14a4f7","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/Projects","sessionId":"473348c5-5f94-4e4d-9ad9-c7e9dd10b438","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"jusprin-newui","slug":"glimmering-doodling-lovelace"}
{"parentUuid":"6f849446-1233-4b45-8367-650ff135abdb","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"7e1818b2-a86b-46e5-abf5-d2df9e7fae27","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CoTAgKAsSmKRrCcbTs1PdF","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Google OAuth sign-in blocked in embedded webview disallowed_useragent WKWebView\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Recep Baltaş\",\"url\":\"https://xenforo.com/community/threads/google-take-action-to-continue-using-googles-oauth-authorization-endpoint.209428\"},{\"title\":\"Posted by Badi Azad, Group Product Manager (@badiazad)\",\"url\":\"https://goo.gle/3h0GhPw\"},{\"title\":\"Upcoming security changes to Google's OAuth 2.0 authorization endpoint in embedded webviews\",\"url\":\"https://developers.googleblog.com/upcoming-security-changes-to-googles-oauth-20-authorization-endpoint-in-embedded-webviews/\"},{\"title\":\"Upcoming security changes to Google's OAuth 2.0 authorization endpoint in embedded webviews\",\"url\":\"https://developers.googleblog.com/en/upcoming-security-changes-to-googles-oauth-20-authorization-endpoint-in-embedded-webviews/\"},{\"title\":\"Upcoming security changes to Google's OAuth 2.0 authorization endpoint in embedded webviews\",\"url\":\"https://developers.googleblog.com/2021/06/upcoming-security-changes-to-googles-oauth-2.0-authorization-endpoint.html\"},{\"title\":\"Upcoming security changes to Google's OAuth 2.0 authorization endpoint in embedded webviews\",\"url\":\"https://developers.googleblog.com/2021/06/upcoming-security-changes-to-googles-oauth-2.0-authorization-endpoint.html?m=1\"},{\"title\":\"June 29, 2021\",\"url\":\"https://goo.gle/3B8pLoz\"}]\n\nGoogle blocks OAuth sign-in from embedded webviews, and WKWebView is one of the named examples. Requests from these views get a `disallowed_useragent` error.\n\n- **Scope:** Google's developer blog says embedded webviews implementing or extending WKWebView, or the deprecated UIWebView, do not comply with Google's secure browser policy. Android's android.webkit.WebView is treated the same way.\n- **Timeline:** The original announcement set a block date of September 30, 2021. A later notice, reposted on a forum, gives February 6, 2023. I couldn't confirm that second date on Google's own site, so treat it with caution.\n- **Why:** Google's rationale is that embedded views can modify or intercept network requests, which is why it treats them as a security risk.\n- **Fix:** Google recommends opening sign-in in the system browser instead. For iOS and macOS, it suggests SFSafariViewController, and for Android, Android Custom Tabs.\n- **Workaround limits:** The `ack_webview_shutdown` parameter only suppresses the warning message. It does not make the flow work, and the forum notice says suppression of the user-facing warning message is not supported.\n\nPractical takeaway: if sign-in is failing in a WKWebView, move the Google sign-in step out of the webview and into SFSafariViewController or ASWebAuthenticationSession. I didn't search for the specific SDK APIs, so verify those in the official docs.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"e37b6bfb-d108-447e-9cba-6c70dcb183d6","timestamp":"2026-11-06T14:42:59.931Z","toolUseResult":{"query":"Google OAuth sign-in blocked in embedded webview disallowed_useragent WKWebView","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01EvWhLsqP9t35bDaoJteCv6","content":[{"title":"Recep Baltaş","url":"https://xenforo.com/community/threads/google-take-action-to-continue-using-googles-oauth-authorization-endpoint.209428"},{"title":"Posted by Badi Azad, Group Product Manager (@badiazad)","url":"https://goo.gle/3h0GhPw"},{"title":"Upcoming security changes to Google's OAuth 2.0 authorization endpoint in embedded webviews","url":"https://developers.googleblog.com/upcoming-security-changes-to-googles-oauth-20-authorization-endpoint-in-embedded-webviews/"},{"title":"Upcoming security changes to Google's OAuth 2.0 authorization endpoint in embedded webviews","url":"https://developers.googleblog.com/en/upcoming-security-changes-to-googles-oauth-20-authorization-endpoint-in-embedded-webviews/"},{"title":"Upcoming security changes to Google's OAuth 2.0 authorization endpoint in embedded webviews","url":"https://developers.googleblog.com/2021/06/upcoming-security-changes-to-googles-oauth-2.0-authorization-endpoint.html"},{"title":"Upcoming security changes to Google's OAuth 2.0 authorization endpoint in embedded webviews","url":"https://developers.googleblog.com/2021/06/upcoming-security-changes-to-googles-oauth-2.0-authorization-endpoint.html?m=1"},{"title":"June 29, 2021","url":"https://goo.gle/3B8pLoz"}]},"Google blocks OAuth sign-in from embedded webviews, and WKWebView is one of the named examples. Requests from these views get a `disallowed_useragent` error.\n\n- **Scope:** Google's developer blog says embedded webviews implementing or extending WKWebView, or the deprecated UIWebView, do not comply with Google's secure browser policy. Android's android.webkit.WebView is treated the same way.\n- **Timeline:** The original announcement set a block date of September 30, 2021. A later notice, reposted on a forum, gives February 6, 2023. I couldn't confirm that second date on Google's own site, so treat it with caution.\n- **Why:** Google's rationale is that embedded views can modify or intercept network requests, which is why it treats them as a security risk.\n- **Fix:** Google recommends opening sign-in in the system browser instead. For iOS and macOS, it suggests SFSafariViewController, and for Android, Android Custom Tabs.\n- **Workaround limits:** The `ack_webview_shutdown` parameter only suppresses the warning message. It does not make the flow work, and the forum notice says suppression of the user-facing warning message is not supported.\n\nPractical takeaway: if sign-in is failing in a WKWebView, move the Google sign-in step out of the webview and into SFSafariViewController or ASWebAuthenticationSession. I didn't search for the specific SDK APIs, so verify those in the official docs."],"durationSeconds":9.629002000000007,"searchCount":1},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"6f849446-1233-4b45-8367-650ff135abdb","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/Projects","sessionId":"473348c5-5f94-4e4d-9ad9-c7e9dd10b438","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"jusprin-newui","slug":"glimmering-doodling-lovelace"}
