{"parentUuid":"33aca751-7630-43b1-ac8b-a4ec298cd4be","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"7e1818b2-a86b-46e5-abf5-d2df9e7fae27","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0198M8ijK4aM598WpUJ7pT7f","type":"tool_result","content":"(eval):1: no matches found: --include=*.py\n/Users/kenneth/.claude/projects/-Users-kenneth-Projects-JusPrin/memory/credits-one-kind-no-ceiling.md:24:Later the same evening Kenneth reviewed every mechanism that was mine, not his. Kept: the launch offer, \"About 25 credits left\" (credits, not messages), \"Expiring credits are used first\", the savings switch on by default, the Account page shape, Standard as the default tier after the first month, the v1 welcome-back fill-ins, the print-report form details, the alias ids. Dropped: the reverse savings alert and board 7c, the month-end and 7-day expiry notices, the daily cap on free app turns, the thinking picker on Standard. Expiry: every expiring lot expires one month from the day it was granted, never at a calendar month end. His message was only a keep list, so anything left off it counts as dropped. A session wrongly called the report rules \"neither kept nor dropped\"; he corrected that the same day: \"I thought the clawback are removed, rigth? And why is it still a placeholder?\" The clawback is removed. Asked about 25 credits, three a day and stopping after two invalid reports, he ruled: \"Remove these. only keep the 1st one\". A report earns 25 credits, one per G-code, and a review is only recorded.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"cf400af8-dfe3-420f-84bc-747be3ccdf3b","timestamp":"2026-11-06T14:43:02.543Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"(eval):1: no matches found: --include=*.py\n/Users/kenneth/.claude/projects/-Users-kenneth-Projects-JusPrin/memory/credits-one-kind-no-ceiling.md:24:Later the same evening Kenneth reviewed every mechanism that was mine, not his. Kept: the launch offer, \"About 25 credits left\" (credits, not messages), \"Expiring credits are used first\", the savings switch on by default, the Account page shape, Standard as the default tier after the first month, the v1 welcome-back fill-ins, the print-report form details, the alias ids. Dropped: the reverse savings alert and board 7c, the month-end and 7-day expiry notices, the daily cap on free app turns, the thinking picker on Standard. Expiry: every expiring lot expires one month from the day it was granted, never at a calendar month end. His message was only a keep list, so anything left off it counts as dropped. A session wrongly called the report rules \"neither kept nor dropped\"; he corrected that the same day: \"I thought the clawback are removed, rigth? And why is it still a placeholder?\" The clawback is removed. Asked about 25 credits, three a day and stopping after two invalid reports, he ruled: \"Remove these. only keep the 1st one\". A report earns 25 credits, one per G-code, and a review is only recorded.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"33aca751-7630-43b1-ac8b-a4ec298cd4be","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/tsd-enterprise","sessionId":"473348c5-5f94-4e4d-9ad9-c7e9dd10b438","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"jusprin-newui","slug":"glimmering-doodling-lovelace"}
