{"parentUuid":"22cbbf6f-2185-4e19-842e-9406f36a0bb2","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgmrNLrtcW6k87S9gXUVX","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1700,"cache_read_input_tokens":227237,"output_tokens":1067,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":35},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1700,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1067,"cache_read_input_tokens":227237,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1700,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1700},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":7529,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgmrNLbHANbRYMAuHGKEa","requestRef":"f0e8b387-b18e-4940-a4c0-b18f8bb91d04","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","attributionMcpServer":"ccd_turn","attributionMcpTool":"wrap_up","type":"assistant","uuid":"5e510ce9-fd66-4664-afef-bbbe9749158e","timestamp":"2026-11-06T14:43:33.473Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/tsd-enterprise","sessionId":"473348c5-5f94-4e4d-9ad9-c7e9dd10b438","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"jusprin-newui","slug":"glimmering-doodling-lovelace"}
{"parentUuid":"5e510ce9-fd66-4664-afef-bbbe9749158e","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgmrNLrtcW6k87S9gXUVX","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**The external browser.** No technical reason forces it. I assumed it because \"Get more credits\" opens the default browser today, and I never questioned that. An in-app sheet is better for the person: they never leave the app, and the app sees checkout finish right away. It can close the sheet, add the credits and turn Send back on, with no \"go back to JusPrin\" step.\n\nIt also takes care of the wrong-account problem more simply. The app can open the sheet already signed in as its own account, so a one-time sign-in link is no longer needed for buying.\n\nThe app can already do this. It shows web pages inside its own windows on Mac, Windows and Linux, and the Agent pane and OrcaSlicer's Bambu login dialog both use them.\n\nWhat an in-app sheet costs, as far as I could check:\n- **Google sign-in doesn't work inside an app's web view.** Google blocks it on purpose ([Google's announcement](https://developers.googleblog.com/2021/06/upcoming-security-changes-to-googles-oauth-2.0-authorization-endpoint.html)). This only matters when someone is signed out. The welcome's \"See prices\" can show the prices and leave signing in to the app's own sign-in.\n- **Chargebee's checkout inside a web view.** Chargebee supports this: it ships a wrapper that puts its checkout in a mobile app's web view ([Chargebee docs](https://chargebee.com/checkout-portal-docs/react-native-wrapper-for-mobile.html)). Its rule that digital goods must use in-app purchases is about iPhone and Android apps, not a desktop app downloaded from our site. What I couldn't confirm is whether the extra bank check some cards need (the one that pops up a bank page) works inside the sheet. We'd need to test that with a test card.\n- **Saved cards (my guess, not tested).** Cards saved in Chrome and password-manager browser extensions probably won't fill in inside the sheet. An \"Open in browser\" link in the sheet covers people who want that.\n\n**The launch offer.** You're right. Doubling only the one-time purchase makes it beat both plans. $10 would buy 1,000 credits that never expire, against Hobby's 750 a month that expire, so nobody has a reason to subscribe during the launch.\n\n**Decision needed: what should the launch offer double?** My pick is to double the first payment of any choice: a one-time purchase gives 1,000, Hobby's first month 1,500, and Workshop's first month 2,000. The cost is capped at one payment per person, and the plans keep their edge. The alternative is to double every month of a plan until the offer ends, which costs more and pulls in people who only came for the bonus. What should the offer double?\n\n**The name.** I'd call it a **credit pack**: \"Credit pack · $10 once · 1,000 credits that never expire\". It names a thing you buy and stands apart from the two plans. \"Top-up\" sounds like an add-on for people who already have a plan. \"Buy credits\" is fine as a button label but doesn't work as a card title. Someone who has bought packs but has no plan would read \"No plan\" in Account. Should the card be called \"Credit pack\"?"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1700,"cache_read_input_tokens":227237,"output_tokens":1067,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":35},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1700,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1067,"cache_read_input_tokens":227237,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1700,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1700},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgmrNLbHANbRYMAuHGKEa","requestRef":"f0e8b387-b18e-4940-a4c0-b18f8bb91d04","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","attributionMcpServer":"ccd_turn","attributionMcpTool":"wrap_up","type":"assistant","uuid":"555d01ab-a9ee-488b-b392-f5728b7dead6","timestamp":"2026-11-06T14:43:36.927Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/tsd-enterprise","sessionId":"473348c5-5f94-4e4d-9ad9-c7e9dd10b438","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"jusprin-newui","slug":"glimmering-doodling-lovelace"}
